+# dup-finder
+
+Find duplicate files by hash to identify wasted disk space. Uses a two-pass approach for fast scanning: first groups files by size, then hashes only the candidates.
+
+## Features
+
+- Two-pass algorithm (size grouping → hash comparison) for fast scanning
+- Configurable hash algorithm (MD5, SHA1, SHA256)
+- Minimum file size filter
+- Automatic exclusion of common directories (.git, node_modules, etc.)
+- JSON output format support
+- Human-readable size formatting
+- Symlink handling
+
+## Installation
+
+```bash
+pip install dup-finder
+```
+
+Or install from source:
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/dup-finder.git
+cd dup-finder
+pip install -e .
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```
+dupfinder [PATHS...] [OPTIONS]
+```
+
+### Examples
+
+```bash
+# Scan a directory
+dupfinder ~/Documents
+
+# Scan multiple paths
+dupfinder /path1 /path2 /path3
+
+# Only check files larger than 1MB
+dupfinder . --min-size 1M
+
+# Use faster MD5 hashing
+dupfinder . --algorithm md5
+
+# JSON output
+dupfinder . --json
+
+# Save results to file
+dupfinder . -o duplicates.txt
+
+# Exclude additional directories
+dupfinder . --exclude cache --exclude tmp
+```
+
+### Example Output
+
+```
+Group #1 (2.4 MB, 3 files)
+  Hash: a3f2c8d1e9b7...
+    /home/user/photos/vacation/img_001.jpg
+    /home/user/backup/img_001.jpg
+    /home/user/old/photos/img_001.jpg
+
+Group #2 (156 KB, 2 files)
+  Hash: b7e4a2f6c3d8...
+    /home/user/downloads/report.pdf
+    /home/user/documents/report.pdf
+
+============================================================
+Found 2 group(s) of duplicate files
+Total duplicate files: 3
+Potential space savings: 5.1 MB
+```
