 # json-path
 
-Extract values from JSON using simple dot-notation paths.
-
-```
-echo '{"users":[{"name":"Alice","age":30}]}' | json-path -p 'users[0].name' -r
-# Output: Alice
-```
+Extract values from JSON using simple path expressions.
 
 ## Features
 
-- Dot-notation paths: `a.b.c`
-- Array indexing: `arr[0]`, `arr[-1]` (negative indices)
-- Wildcard arrays: `arr[*]` returns all elements
-- Optional `$` root prefix: `$users[0].name`
+- Dot notation: `a.b.c`
+- Array indexing: `a[0]`, `a[-1]`
+- Wildcards: `a[*]` (all elements)
+- Slices: `a[0:2]` (start:end, exclusive)
+- Filters: `a[?foo]` (match keys/values containing "foo")
 - Read from file or stdin
-- Raw output mode (`-r`) for unformatted values
-- Quiet mode (`-q`) to suppress error messages
 
 ## Install
 
