+# healthcheck-api
+
+REST API for monitoring URL health status with configurable check intervals.
+
+Add URLs to monitor, check them on demand, and track their health history. Built with Node.js and Express — no database required, all data stored in memory.
+
+## Features
+
+- One-time URL health checks via API
+- Persistent monitors with configurable intervals
+- Response time tracking
+- Health history (last 100 checks per monitor)
+- Timeout support per monitor
+- Zero dependencies (uses Node.js built-in http/https)
+
+## Install
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/healthcheck-api.git
+cd healthcheck-api
+npm install express
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+Start the server:
+```bash
+npm start
+# or
+node server.js
+```
+
+Server runs on port 3000 by default. Set `PORT` env var to change:
+```bash
+PORT=8080 npm start
+```
+
+## API Endpoints
+
+### GET /
+
+Returns API info and available endpoints.
+
+### POST /health/check
+
+One-time health check of a URL.
+
+```bash
+curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/health/check \
+  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
+  -d '{"url": "https://httpbin.org/get", "timeout": 5000}'
+```
+
+Response:
+```json
+{
+  "url": "https://httpbin.org/get",
+  "statusCode": 200,
+  "responseTime": 342,
+  "status": "healthy",
+  "lastCheck": "2026-05-28T12:00:00.000Z",
+  "headers": {
+    "server": "gunicorn",
+    "contentType": "application/json"
+  }
+}
+```
+
+### POST /monitors
+
+Add a URL to monitor with periodic checks.
+
+```bash
+curl -X POST http://localhost:3000/monitors \
+  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
+  -d '{"name": "my-api", "url": "https://api.example.com/health", "timeout": 3000, "interval": 30000}'
+```
+
