+# Rate Limiter API
+
+In-memory rate limiting API using the token bucket algorithm. Define policies, check limits, and monitor usage via REST endpoints.
+
+## Features
+
+- Token bucket algorithm with configurable refill rates
+- Multiple independent policies
+- Per-identifier tracking (IP, user ID, API key, etc.)
+- Standard rate limit headers (`X-RateLimit-Limit`, `X-RateLimit-Remaining`, `X-RateLimit-Reset`)
+- HTTP 429 responses with `Retry-After` when limits are exceeded
+- In-memory storage (no external dependencies)
+- Thread-safe concurrent access
+
+## Quick Start
+
+```bash
+go run .
+```
+
+Server starts on `http://localhost:8080`.
+
+## API Endpoints
+
+### Health Check
+
+```
+GET /health
+```
+
+### Create Policy
+
+```
+POST /policies
+Content-Type: application/json
+
+{
+  "key": "api",
+  "max_tokens": 100,
+  "refill_rate": 10,
+  "refill_interval_seconds": 60
+}
+```
+
+### List Policies
+
+```
+GET /policies
+```
+
+### Get Policy
+
+```
+GET /policies/:key
+```
+
+### Delete Policy
+
+```
+DELETE /policies/:key
+```
+
+### Check Rate Limit
+
+```
+GET /check?policy=api&identifier=user123
+```
+
+Returns `200` if allowed (consumes a token), or `429` if rate limited.
+
+### Check Status (no token consumed)
+
+```
+GET /status?policy=api&identifier=user123
+```
+
+### Reset Bucket
+
