 # log-rotate
 
-Log rotation utility for the command line. Rotates log files based on size, age, or schedule with optional gzip compression and configurable backup retention.
+A configurable log rotation utility written in Go. Automatically rotates, compresses, and cleans up log files based on size, age, and retention policies.
 
 ## Features
 
-- **Size-based rotation** — rotate when log exceeds a threshold (default 100MB)
-- **Age-based cleanup** — delete rotated logs older than N days
-- **Schedule-based rotation** — daily or weekly rotation regardless of size
-- **Gzip compression** — automatically compress rotated logs
-- **Backup retention** — keep a configurable number of backup files
-- **Dry run mode** — preview what would happen without making changes
-- **Config file support** — JSON config for cron/automated use
-- **Directory scanning** — automatically find `.log` files in directories
+- Rotate log files exceeding a configurable size threshold
+- Optional gzip compression of rotated logs
+- Automatic cleanup of old backups beyond retention limit
+- Minimum age policy to avoid rotating recently modified files
+- Dry-run mode for safe testing
+- Verbose output for debugging
+- Configurable file extension matching
+- Zero external dependencies (pure Go standard library)
+- Docker support
 
