+# process-tree
+
+Display a tree view of running processes in the terminal, with colored output, filtering, and resource usage statistics.
+
+## Features
+
+- **Process tree** — Hierarchical view of all running processes with tree connectors
+- **Flat list** — Sortable, filterable list of all processes
+- **Find** — Locate a process by PID and show its ancestry chain
+- **Top** — Top N processes by CPU or memory usage with bar chart
+- **Count** — Process count summary grouped by user
+- **Colored output** — CPU/memory usage color-coded by severity
+
+## Install
+
+```bash
+# Clone and link
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/process-tree.git
+cd process-tree
+npm link
+
+# Or install globally
+npm install -g process-tree
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```
+process-tree [command] [options]
+```
+
+### Commands
+
+| Command | Description |
+|---------|-------------|
+| `(no command)` | Show full process tree (default) |
+| `tree [-d DEPTH]` | Show process tree with optional depth limit |
+| `flat [filter]` | Show flat list of processes (filterable) |
+| `find <PID>` | Show process and its ancestry |
+| `top [N] [cpu\|mem]` | Show top N processes by CPU or memory |
+| `count` | Show process count summary |
+
+## Examples
+
+```bash
+# Full process tree
+process-tree
+
+# Tree limited to 3 levels
+process-tree tree -d 3
+
+# Flat list of all processes
+process-tree flat
+
+# Filter processes by name
+process-tree flat node
+process-tree flat root
+
+# Find a specific process and show its ancestry
+process-tree find 1234
+
+# Top 10 processes by CPU
+process-tree top 10 cpu
+
+# Top 5 processes by memory
+process-tree top 5 mem
+
+# Process count summary
+process-tree count
+```
+
+## Requirements
+
+- Node.js 14+
+- Linux (uses `ps` command)
+
+## License
+
