+# git-log-visual
+
+Visualize git history as colored ASCII art in the terminal. Compact logs, graphs, statistics, timelines, and heatmaps.
+
+## Features
+
+- **Compact log** — Colorful commit log with author color-coding and branch tags
+- **Graph view** — ASCII graph with colored dots showing branch topology
+- **Statistics** — Contributor breakdown, monthly activity, and bus factor analysis
+- **Timeline** — Commits grouped by date for easy chronological browsing
+- **Heatmap** — 90-day commit heatmap inspired by GitHub's contribution graph
+
+## Install
+
+```bash
+# Clone and link
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/git-log-visual.git
+cd git-log-visual
+npm link
+
+# Or install globally
+npm install -g git-log-visual
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```
+git-log-visual [command] [options] [path]
+```
+
+### Commands
+
+| Command | Description |
+|---------|-------------|
+| `compact [N]` | Compact colored log (default, max N commits) |
+| `graph [N]` | ASCII graph with colored dots |
+| `stats` | Repository statistics and contributor breakdown |
+| `timeline [N]` | Commits grouped by date |
+| `heatmap` | Commit heatmap for last 90 days |
+
+## Examples
+
+```bash
+# Compact log (default, 30 commits)
+git-log-visual
+
+# Show 50 commits
+git-log-visual compact 50
+
+# Graph view, 20 commits
+git-log-visual graph 20
+
+# Repository statistics
+git-log-visual stats
+
+# Timeline view
+git-log-visual timeline
+
+# Commit heatmap
+git-log-visual heatmap
+
+# Stats for a specific repo
+git-log-visual stats /path/to/repo
+```
+
+## Requirements
+
+- Node.js 14+
+- Git (must be run inside a git repository or provide a repo path)
+
+## License
+
+MIT
