@@ -0,0 +1,118 @@
+# docker-logs-cli
+
+Aggregate, filter, and display Docker container logs from multiple containers in a single colored terminal output.
+
+## Features
+
+- **Multi-container logs**: View logs from all running containers or select specific ones
+- **Colored output**: Log levels (ERROR, WARN, INFO, DEBUG) are automatically detected and colorized
+- **Level filtering**: Filter by log level (`--level error`, `--level warn`, etc.)
+- **Regex grep**: Filter log lines with regex patterns (`--grep "timeout"`)
+- **Stream filtering**: Show only stdout or stderr (`--stream stderr`)
+- **Follow mode**: Real-time log streaming with `-f` / `--follow`
+- **Tail support**: Show last N lines with `-t` / `--tail`
+- **Since filter**: Show logs from a duration ago with `--since 30m`
+- **Graceful shutdown**: Ctrl+C stops all log streams cleanly
+
+## Installation
+
+### From source
+
+```bash
+go install github.com/TataneSan/docker-logs-cli@latest
+```
+
+### Build manually
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/docker-logs-cli.git
+cd docker-logs-cli
+go build -o docker-logs-cli .
+sudo mv docker-logs-cli /usr/local/bin/
+```
+
+### Docker
+
+```bash
+docker run --rm -v /var/run/docker.sock:/var/run/docker.sock \
+  tatanesan/docker-logs-cli --help
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```
+docker-logs-cli [OPTIONS] [CONTAINER...]
+```
+
+### Options
+
+| Flag | Description |
+|------|-------------|
+| `-f, --follow` | Follow log output in real-time |
+| `-l, --level LEVEL` | Filter by log level (`info`, `warn`, `error`, `debug`) |
+| `-s, --since DUR` | Show logs since duration (e.g. `10m`, `2h`, `1h30m`) |
+| `-t, --tail N` | Number of lines from the end (default: all) |
+| `-g, --grep PATTERN` | Filter logs matching regex pattern |
+| `--stream STREAM` | Filter by stream: `stdout`, `stderr`, `all` (default: all) |
