+# jq-lite
+
+Lightweight JSON query tool for the terminal. Query JSON data using dot notation, array indexing, slicing, and filtering — without the complexity of full jq.
+
+## Features
+
+- **Dot notation**: `.key`, `.key.subkey` for nested access
+- **Array operations**: `[0]`, `[*]`, `[start:end]` indexing and slicing
+- **Iteration**: `.items[].field` to extract fields from array elements
+- **Functions**: `keys()`, `length`, `type`, `select()`, `sort_by()`, `map()`
+- **Filtering**: `select(.field > 0)` to filter array elements
+- **Pipe support**: read from stdin for use in shell pipelines
+- **Output modes**: pretty-printed (default), compact (`-c`), raw strings (`-r`)
+
+## Install
+
+```bash
+go install github.com/TataneSan/jq-lite@latest
+```
+
+Or build from source:
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/jq-lite.git
+cd jq-lite
+go build -o jq-lite .
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```
+jq-lite [options] <file> <expression>
+cat file.json | jq-lite <expression>
+```
+
+### Options
+
+| Flag | Description |
+|------|-------------|
+| `-c`, `--compact` | Compact output (single line per result) |
+| `-r`, `--raw` | Raw output (print strings without quotes) |
+| `-h`, `--help` | Show help message |
+
+## Examples
+
+### Field access
+
+```bash
+# Single field
+jq-lite data.json .name
+
+# Nested field
+jq-lite config.json .database.host
+
+# Raw string output
+jq-lite -r data.json .name
+```
+
+### Array operations
+
+```bash
+# First element
+jq-lite data.json '.items[0]'
+
+# All elements
+jq-lite data.json '.items[*]'
+
+# Slice (first 3 elements)
+jq-lite data.json '.items[0:3]'
+
+# Extract field from each element
+jq-lite data.json '.users[].email'
+```
+
+### Functions
+
+```bash
+# List object keys
