+# env-schema
+
+Validate `.env` files against a YAML schema. Catches missing required variables, type mismatches, out-of-range values, and pattern violations before they cause runtime errors.
+
+## Features
+
+- **Type validation**: `string`, `integer`, `float`, `boolean`
+- **Required/optional** with defaults
+- **Enum constraints**: restrict values to an allowed list
+- **Numeric ranges**: `min` / `max` for integers and floats
+- **String length**: `min_length` / `max_length`
+- **Regex patterns**: arbitrary `pattern` matching
+- **Multiple env files**: load base + override files (later files win)
+- **Example generation**: `env-schema example` produces a ready-to-fill `.env`
+- **List variables**: `env-schema list` shows all schema variables with metadata
+
+## Install
+
+```bash
+go install github.com/TataneSan/env-schema@latest
+```
+
+Or build from source:
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/env-schema.git
+cd env-schema
+go build -o env-schema .
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```
+env-schema <command> [arguments]
+
+Commands:
+  validate <schema.yaml> [envfile...]  Validate env file(s) against schema
+  check    <schema.yaml> [envfile...]  Alias for validate
+  list     <schema.yaml>               List all variables defined in schema
+  example  <schema.yaml>               Generate example .env from schema
+```
+
+If no env file is specified, `.env` in the current directory is used. Multiple env files can be provided; later files override earlier ones.
+
+## Schema Format
+
+Define a YAML file with a `variables` map. Each key is an environment variable name:
+
+```yaml
+variables:
+  DATABASE_URL:
+    type: string
+    required: true
+    description: "PostgreSQL connection string"
+
+  PORT:
+    type: integer
+    required: false
+    default: "3000"
+    min: 1024
+    max: 65535
+
+  LOG_LEVEL:
+    type: string
+    required: false
+    default: "info"
+    enum:
+      - debug
+      - info
+      - warn
+      - error
+
+  API_KEY:
+    type: string
+    required: true
+    pattern: "^[A-Za-z0-9]{32}$"
+    min_length: 32
+    max_length: 32
