+# systemd-once
+
+Create and manage systemd one-shot services from the command line. Simplifies running commands through systemd with automatic journal logging, status tracking, and service lifecycle management.
+
+## Features
+
+- **new** — Create a one-shot systemd service unit from a command
+- **run** — Start a service and display its journal output
+- **logs** — Follow journal logs for a service
+- **status** — Check service status
+- **remove** — Delete a service unit and reload systemd
+- **list** — List all registered one-shot services
+
+Supports both system-level and user-level services.
+
+## Installation
+
+```bash
+go install github.com/TataneSan/systemd-once@latest
+```
+
+Or build from source:
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/systemd-once.git
+cd systemd-once
+go build -o systemd-once .
+sudo cp systemd-once /usr/local/bin/
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```
+systemd-once <command> [arguments] [flags]
+```
+
+### Commands
+
+| Command | Description |
+|---------|-------------|
+| `new <name> <command>` | Create a new one-shot service |
+| `run <name>` | Run a service and show output |
+| `logs <name>` | Follow service logs |
+| `status <name>` | Show service status |
+| `remove <name>` | Remove a service |
+| `list` | List all services |
+
+### Flags
+
+| Flag | Description |
+|------|-------------|
+| `-desc string` | Service description |
+| `-after string` | After directive (default: `network.target`) |
+| `-dir string` | Working directory |
+| `-user-run string` | Run as user |
+| `-group string` | Run as group |
+| `-env string` | Environment variable (KEY=VALUE) |
+| `--user` | Use user-level services |
+| `-f` | Force operation without confirmation |
+| `-reload` | Daemon-reload before executing |
+
+### Examples
+
+Create a daily backup service:
+
+```bash
+systemd-once new daily-backup "tar czf /backup/data-\$(date +%F).tar.gz /data" \
+  -desc "Daily data backup" -user root
+```
+
+Run it and see the output:
+
+```bash
+systemd-once run daily-backup -reload
+```
+
+Create a service with environment variables:
+
