+# expense-report
+
+Generate expense reports from CSV files with grouping, filtering, and multiple output formats.
+
+## Features
+
+- Read expenses from CSV files
+- Group by category or date
+- Filter by date range
+- Multiple output formats: text, JSON, CSV
+- Configurable column mapping
+- Currency display
+- Summary statistics (total, count, average)
+
+## Installation
+
+### From source
+
+```bash
+go install github.com/TataneSan/expense-report@latest
+```
+
+### Build manually
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/expense-report.git
+cd expense-report
+go build -o expense-report .
+sudo mv expense-report /usr/local/bin/
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```
+expense-report [OPTIONS] INPUT.CSV
+```
+
+### Options
+
+| Flag | Description | Default |
+|------|-------------|---------|
+| `-f, --format FORMAT` | Output format: text, json, csv | `text` |
+| `-g, --group GROUP` | Group by: date, category | `category` |
+| `-d, --start DATE` | Start date filter (YYYY-MM-DD) | - |
+| `-e, --end DATE` | End date filter (YYYY-MM-DD) | - |
+| `-c, --currency CODE` | Currency code for display | `EUR` |
+| `-o, --output FILE` | Output file (default: stdout) | - |
+| `--no-header` | Input CSV has no header row | `false` |
+| `--date-col NUM` | Column index for date | `0` |
+| `--cat-col NUM` | Column index for category | `1` |
+| `--desc-col NUM` | Column index for description | `2` |
+| `--amt-col NUM` | Column index for amount | `3` |
+| `--version` | Show version | - |
+| `-h, --help` | Show help | - |
+
+### CSV Format
+
+Default columns: `date,category,description,amount`
+
+Example CSV:
+```csv
+date,category,description,amount
+2024-01-15,Food,Groceries,45.50
+2024-01-16,Transport,Bus pass,30.00
+2024-01-17,Food,Lunch,12.50
+```
+
+### Examples
+
+Generate a text report grouped by category:
+```bash
+expense-report expenses.csv
+```
+
+Group by date:
+```bash
+expense-report -g date expenses.csv
+```
