+# net-latency
+
+Network latency measurement tool. Probe hosts using TCP connections and HTTP requests, with statistics (min, max, avg, p95).
+
+## Install
+
+```bash
+go install github.com/TataneSan/net-latency@latest
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```
+net-latency <host> [port] [flags]
+net-latency http://<url> [flags]
+```
+
+### Flags
+
+| Flag | Default | Description |
+|------|---------|-------------|
+| `-c` | `4` | Number of probes |
+| `-t` | `5s` | Connection timeout |
+| `-q` | `false` | Only print summary |
+
+### Examples
+
+```bash
+# TCP probe on default port 80
+net-latency google.com
+
+# TCP probe on specific port
+net-latency 8.8.8.8 53
+
+# HTTP probe
+net-latency https://google.com
+
+# More probes with custom timeout
+net-latency google.com 443 -c 10 -t 3s
+
+# Quiet mode (summary only)
+net-latency google.com -q
+```
+
+### Output
+
+```
+[OK] google.com (TCP) - 23ms
+[OK] google.com (TCP) - 21ms
+[OK] google.com (TCP) - 24ms
+[OK] google.com (TCP) - 22ms
+
+HOST        PORT  PROTOCOL  ATTEMPTS  OK  MIN   MAX   AVG   P95
+----        ----  --------  --------  --  ---   ---   ---   ---
+google.com  80    TCP       4         4   21ms  24ms  22ms  24ms
+```
+
+## Exit Codes
+
+- `0`: At least one probe succeeded
+- `1`: All probes failed or invalid arguments
+
+## License
+
+MIT
