+# log-api
+
+Simple logging API with filtering and stats. Store log entries, query by level/source, and get aggregate statistics.
+
+## Features
+
+- Add log entries with level, message, source, and extra data
+- Filter logs by level (debug, info, warn, error) and source
+- Pagination support (limit/offset)
+- Stats endpoint with counts per level
+- Purge old entries by age
+- In-memory storage with automatic caps
+
+## API Endpoints
+
+| Method | Endpoint | Description |
+|--------|----------|-------------|
+| `GET` | `/api/health` | Health check |
+| `POST` | `/api/logs` | Add a log entry |
+| `GET` | `/api/logs?level=&source=&limit=50&offset=0` | Get logs with filters |
+| `GET` | `/api/logs/stats` | Get log counts by level |
+| `DELETE` | `/api/logs?hours=24` | Purge entries older than N hours |
+
+## Install
+
+```bash
+go build -o log-api .
+./log-api
+```
+
+Or with Docker:
+
+```bash
+docker build -t log-api .
+docker run -p 8080:8080 log-api
+```
+
+## Configuration
+
+| Environment Variable | Default | Description |
+|---------------------|---------|-------------|
+| `PORT` | `8080` | Server port |
+
+## Usage Examples
+
+### Add a log entry
+
+```bash
+curl -X POST http://localhost:8080/api/logs \
+  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
+  -d '{"level":"error","msg":"connection timeout","source":"database"}'
+```
+
+Response:
+```json
+{
+  "id": "a1b2c3d4-...",
+  "level": "error",
+  "msg": "connection timeout",
+  "source": "database",
+  "extra": "",
+  "ts": "2026-05-28T12:00:00Z"
+}
+```
+
+### Filter logs
+
+```bash
+# By level
+curl "http://localhost:8080/api/logs?level=error"
+
+# By source
+curl "http://localhost:8080/api/logs?source=database"
+
+# With pagination
+curl "http://localhost:8080/api/logs?limit=10&offset=20"
+```
+
