+# Status API
+
+Configurable service status API with a live dashboard. Monitor HTTP endpoints and TCP ports, expose health status via REST, and get a real-time HTML dashboard.
+
+## Features
+
+- Monitor HTTP(S) endpoints and TCP ports
+- Configurable check intervals and timeouts per service
+- REST API for managing services at runtime
+- HTML dashboard with auto-refresh
+- Check history (last 20 results per service)
+- Overall status: healthy, degraded, down, unknown
+- CORS enabled
+- Zero external dependencies (Node.js built-in modules only)
+
+## Installation
+
+```bash
+npm install
+```
+
+Or run directly (no dependencies to install):
+
+```bash
+node index.js
+```
+
+## Configuration
+
+Create a `config.json` file (see `config.json` for an example):
+
+```json
+{
+  "defaultInterval": 30000,
+  "defaultTimeout": 5000,
+  "services": [
+    {
+      "name": "my-api",
+      "type": "http",
+      "url": "https://api.example.com/health",
+      "interval": 15000,
+      "timeout": 5000
+    },
+    {
+      "name": "database",
+      "type": "tcp",
+      "host": "localhost",
+      "port": 5432,
+      "interval": 10000,
+      "timeout": 3000
+    }
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+### Environment Variables
+
+| Variable | Default | Description |
+|----------|---------|-------------|
+| `PORT` | `3000` | Server port |
+| `STATUS_CONFIG` | `./config.json` | Path to config file |
+
+## Usage
+
+```bash
+# Start the server
+npm start
+
+# Development mode (auto-reload)
+npm run dev
+
+# Custom port
+PORT=8080 node index.js
+
+# Custom config path
+STATUS_CONFIG=./prod.json node index.js
+```
+
