+# log-compress
+
+Compress and archive log files with configurable retention policies.
+
+## Features
+
+- Compress log files with gzip, zstd, or lz4
+- Filter by glob patterns, size, or age
+- Rotate logs by splitting large files
+- Configure retention policies (keep N files, max age)
+- Dry-run mode to preview changes
+- Verbose output with compression ratios
+
+## Install
+
+```bash
+go install github.com/TataneSan/log-compress@latest
+```
+
+Or download a release from [GitHub Releases](https://github.com/TataneSan/log-compress/releases).
+
+## Usage
+
+```bash
+# Compress all .log files in a directory
+log-compress /var/log/myapp
+
+# Compress with specific pattern and format
+log-compress /var/log -pattern "*.log" -format zstd
+
+# Dry run to preview changes
+log-compress /var/log -dry
+
+# Compress files older than 3 days
+log-compress /var/log -older-than 72h
+
+# Compress files larger than 100MB
+log-compress /var/log -min-size 100MB
+
+# Remove originals after compression
+log-compress /var/log -remove-original
+
+# Verbose output
+log-compress /var/log -v
+```
+
+### Flags
+
+| Flag | Default | Description |
+|------|---------|-------------|
+| `-pattern` | `*.log` | Glob pattern for files to compress |
+| `-format` | `gzip` | Compression format: gzip, zstd, lz4 |
+| `-older-than` | `24h` | Only compress files older than duration |
+| `-min-size` | `0` | Only compress files larger than size |
+| `-remove-original` | `false` | Remove original file after compression |
+| `-dry` | `false` | Dry run — show what would be done |
+| `-v` | `false` | Verbose output |
+
+### Size formats
+
+Sizes accept suffixes: `B`, `KB`, `MB`, `GB` (e.g., `100MB`, `1.5GB`).
+
+### Duration formats
+
+Durations accept Go-style durations: `30m`, `2h`, `72h`, `30h` (e.g., `24h` for one day).
+
+## Examples
+
+### Compress application logs nightly
+
+```bash
+# In a cron job (daily at 2 AM)
+0 2 * * * log-compress /var/log/myapp -older-than 24h -remove-original
+```
+
+### Archive old access logs with zstd
+
+```bash
