+# env-backup
+
+Save and restore .env files with timestamped backups.
+
+## Features
+
+- Create compressed backups of all .env files in a project
+- Restore from any previous backup version
+- List all available backups with metadata
+- Diff current .env files against a backup
+- Add notes to backups for context
+- Supports .env, .env.local, .env.development, .env.production, etc.
+
+## Install
+
+```bash
+go install github.com/TataneSan/env-backup@latest
+```
+
+Or download a release from [GitHub Releases](https://github.com/TataneSan/env-backup/releases).
+
+## Usage
+
+```bash
+# Create a backup
+env-backup save
+
+# Create a backup with a note
+env-backup save -note "before production deploy"
+
+# List all backups
+env-backup list
+
+# Restore the latest backup
+env-backup restore
+
+# Restore a specific backup
+env-backup restore --version 2
+
+# Diff current .env against a backup
+env-backup diff
+env-backup diff --version 1
+
+# Target a specific directory
+env-backup save ../my-project
+```
+
+## Examples
+
+### Before changing environment variables
+
+```bash
+# Save current state
+env-backup save -note "before switching to staging"
+
+# Make your changes to .env files...
+
+# Check what changed
+env-backup diff
+
+# Restore if something went wrong
+env-backup restore
+```
+
+### Before a deployment
+
+```bash
+# Backup production env
+env-backup save -note "pre-deploy 2026-05-28"
+
+# Deploy...
+
+# If needed, restore
+env-backup list
+env-backup restore --version 5
+```
+
+## Supported files
