+# docker-stats-cli
+
+Real-time Docker container stats viewer for the terminal. Displays CPU usage, memory, network I/O, and disk I/O for all running containers in a color-coded table.
+
+![Go](https://img.shields.io/badge/Go-1.21+-00ADD8?style=flat&logo=go)
+![License](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-green.svg)
+
+## Features
+
+- **Real-time streaming** — auto-refreshes at configurable intervals (default: 1s)
+- **Color-coded output** — red for high usage (>80%), yellow for moderate (>50%)
+- **Filter containers** — substring match on container name
+- **Threshold alerts** — configurable CPU and memory alert thresholds
+- **Sorting** — sort by CPU or memory usage
+- **CSV export** — single snapshot export to CSV for further analysis
+- **Single snapshot mode** — one-time capture instead of streaming
+
+## Install
+
+### From source
+
+```bash
+go install github.com/tatanesan/docker-stats-cli@latest
+```
+
+### Build manually
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/docker-stats-cli.git
+cd docker-stats-cli
+go build -o docker-stats-cli .
+sudo mv docker-stats-cli /usr/local/bin/
+```
+
+## Requirements
+
+- Go 1.21+
+- Docker (must be running and accessible)
+
+## Usage
+
+```
+docker-stats-cli [options]
+```
+
+### Options
+
+| Flag | Description | Default |
+|------|-------------|---------|
+| `-f PATTERN` | Filter containers by name (substring) | (all) |
+| `-once` | Single snapshot instead of streaming | false |
+| `-interval DURATION` | Refresh interval | 1s |
+| `-cpu-alert PCT` | CPU usage threshold for alert (0=disabled) | 0 |
+| `-mem-alert PCT` | Memory usage threshold for alert (0=disabled) | 0 |
+| `-sort COLUMN` | Sort by column: `cpu`, `mem` | docker order |
+| `-csv FILE` | Export snapshot to CSV (`-` for stdout) | (none) |
+| `-no-stream` | Don't clear screen between updates | false |
+
+### Examples
+
+Stream all running containers:
+```bash
+docker-stats-cli
+```
+
+Filter containers with "web" in the name:
+```bash
+docker-stats-cli -f web
+```
+
+Single snapshot sorted by CPU:
+```bash
+docker-stats-cli -once -sort cpu
+```
+
+Alert when any container exceeds 80% CPU:
+```bash
+docker-stats-cli -cpu-alert 80
