+# uptime-check
+
+Check service uptime and display a status report. Supports HTTP endpoints, TCP ports, and configurable check intervals.
+
+![Go](https://img.shields.io/badge/Go-1.21+-00ADD8?style=flat&logo=go)
+![License](https://img.shields.io/badge/License-MIT-green.svg)
+
+## Features
+
+- **Multi-protocol checks** — HTTP (with status code validation) and TCP port checks
+- **Configurable thresholds** — custom timeout and "slow" response time threshold
+- **JSON config** — define services in a JSON file for easy management
+- **Continuous monitoring** — repeat checks at a configurable interval
+- **JSON output** — machine-readable output for piping to other tools
+- **Quiet mode** — only report non-ok services
+- **Retries** — automatic retries for transient failures
+- **Exit codes** — exits with code 1 if any service is down (CI-friendly)
+
+## Install
+
+### From source
+
+```bash
+go install github.com/tatanesan/uptime-check@latest
+```
+
+### Build manually
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/uptime-check.git
+cd uptime-check
+go build -o uptime-check .
+sudo mv uptime-check /usr/local/bin/
+```
+
+## Requirements
+
+- Go 1.21+
+
+## Usage
+
+```
+uptime-check [options]
+```
+
+### Options
+
+| Flag | Description | Default |
+|------|-------------|---------|
+| `-config FILE` | Path to JSON config file with services | (none) |
+| `-http URL` | HTTP URL to check (repeatable) | (none) |
+| `-tcp ADDR` | TCP address to check `host:port` (repeatable) | (none) |
+| `-timeout DURATION` | Timeout per check | 5s |
+| `-slow DURATION` | Threshold for "slow" status | 2s |
+| `-retry N` | Number of retries for failed checks | 0 |
+| `-json` | Output results as JSON | false |
+| `-quiet` | Only output non-ok services | false |
+| `-interval DURATION` | Repeat checks at interval (0=once) | 0 (once) |
+
+### Config file format
+
+```json
+[
+  {"name": "Website", "type": "http", "target": "https://example.com"},
+  {"name": "API", "type": "http", "target": "https://api.example.com/health"},
+  {"name": "PostgreSQL", "type": "tcp", "target": "127.0.0.1:5432"},
+  {"name": "Redis", "type": "tcp", "target": "127.0.0.1:6379"}
+]
+```
+
+### Examples
+
+Check a single HTTP endpoint:
+```bash
+uptime-check -http https://example.com
+```
+
+Check multiple endpoints:
