+# reading-notes
+
+Reading notes by book/chapter — track your reading, take chapter notes, and rate books from the terminal.
+
+## Features
+
+- Add books with author information
+- Take notes organized by chapter
+- Tag notes for easy filtering
+- Rate chapters and books (1-5)
+- Mark books as completed
+- Filter notes by chapter or tag
+- Reading statistics overview
+- JSON-based storage in `~/.reading-notes/`
+
+## Install
+
+```bash
+# From source
+go install github.com/TataneSan/reading-notes@latest
+
+# Or build manually
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/reading-notes.git
+cd reading-notes
+go build -o reading-notes .
+cp reading-notes /usr/local/bin/
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```
+reading-notes <command> [arguments]
+```
+
+### Commands
+
+| Command | Description |
+|---------|-------------|
+| `add-book <title>` | Add a new book |
+| `list` | List all books |
+| `note <book> <chapter> <title>` | Add a reading note |
+| `show <book>` | Show notes for a book |
+| `finish <book>` | Mark a book as completed |
+| `rate <book> <rating>` | Rate a book (1-5) |
+| `stats` | Show reading statistics |
+| `delete <book>` | Delete a book |
+
+### Examples
+
+```bash
+# Add a book
+reading-notes add-book "Clean Code" -a "Robert C. Martin"
+
+# Add chapter notes
+reading-notes note "Clean Code" "1" "Functions should be small" -c "Max 4 lines" -t principle
+reading-notes note "Clean Code" "2" "Good names matter" -t naming,clarity -r 4
+
+# Show notes
+reading-notes show "Clean Code"
+reading-notes show "Clean Code" -c 1
+reading-notes show "Clean Code" -t naming
+
+# Rate and finish
+reading-notes rate "Clean Code" 5
+reading-notes finish "Clean Code"
+
+# View statistics
+reading-notes stats
+```
+
+### Add Book Options
+
+- `-a`, `--author` — Book author
+
+### Note Options
+
+- `-c`, `--content` — Note content
+- `-t`, `--tags` — Comma-separated tags
