+# github-trending-cli
+
+A fast CLI tool to display trending GitHub repositories in your terminal. Fetches data from the GitHub Search API and presents it in a clean, readable format.
+
+## Features
+
+- Display trending repositories by **daily**, **weekly**, or **monthly** period
+- Filter by **programming language** (Go, Rust, Python, TypeScript, etc.)
+- Configurable result **limit** (1–25)
+- **JSON output** support for scripting and pipelines
+- **Quiet mode** to suppress headers/footers
+- Relative time formatting ("2 hours ago", "3 days ago")
+- Compact star/fork display (1.2K, 3.5M)
+- No authentication required (30 requests/min unauthenticated)
+- Set `GITHUB_TOKEN` env var for higher rate limits (1000/min)
+
+## Installation
+
+### From source
+
+```bash
+go install github.com/TataneSan/github-trending-cli@latest
+```
+
+### Build manually
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/github-trending-cli.git
+cd github-trending-cli
+go build -o github-trending-cli .
+sudo mv github-trending-cli /usr/local/bin/
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```
+github-trending-cli [flags]
+```
+
+### Flags
+
+| Flag | Alias | Description | Default |
+|------|-------|-------------|---------|
+| `-l` | `--language` | Filter by programming language | all |
+| `-p` | `--period` | Time period: `daily`, `weekly`, `monthly` | `daily` |
+| `-n` | `--limit` | Number of results (1–25) | `10` |
+| `-j` | `--json` | Output as JSON | false |
+| `-q` | `--quiet` | Suppress header and footer | false |
+| `-v` | `--version` | Print version | — |
+
+### Examples
+
+Show daily trending repositories:
+```bash
+github-trending-cli
+```
+
+Show trending Go repositories this week:
+```bash
+github-trending-cli -l Go -p weekly
+```
+
+Show top 20 trending Rust repos as JSON:
+```bash
+github-trending-cli -l Rust -n 20 -j
+```
+
+Show monthly trending with no header/footer:
+```bash
+github-trending-cli -p monthly -q
+```
+
+Pipe JSON output to jq:
+```bash
+github-trending-cli -l TypeScript -j | jq '.[].name'
+```
+
