+# markdown-table
+
+Convert CSV, TSV, or delimited data to properly formatted Markdown tables.
+
+Reads data from a file or stdin and outputs a Markdown table to stdout. Supports automatic delimiter detection, column alignment, and header rows.
+
+## Features
+
+- **Auto-detect** delimiter (comma, tab, pipe, semicolon)
+- **Header row** support with separator line
+- **Column alignment**: left, right, or center
+- Read from **file** or **stdin** (pipe-friendly)
+- Automatic column width calculation
+- Pipe character escaping
+
+## Installation
+
+### From source
+
+```bash
+go install github.com/TataneSan/markdown-table@latest
+```
+
+### Build manually
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/markdown-table.git
+cd markdown-table
+go build -o markdown-table .
+sudo mv markdown-table /usr/local/bin/
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```
+markdown-table [flags] [file]
+```
+
+### Flags
+
+| Flag | Alias | Description | Default |
+|------|-------|-------------|---------|
+| `-d` | `--delimiter` | Field delimiter: `auto`, `comma`, `tab`, `pipe`, `semicolon` | `auto` |
+| `-h` | `--has-header` | First row is a header | `true` |
+| `-a` | `--align` | Column alignment: `left`, `right`, `center` | `left` |
+| `-n` | `--no-border` | Omit the separator line | `false` |
+| `-v` | `--version` | Print version | — |
+
+### Examples
+
+**From stdin (CSV):**
+```bash
+echo "Name,Age,City
+Alice,30,Paris
+Bob,25,Lyon" | markdown-table
+```
+
+Output:
+```markdown
+| Name  | Age | City  |
+| ----- | --- | ----- |
+| Alice | 30  | Paris |
+| Bob   | 25  | Lyon  |
+```
+
+**From a file:**
+```bash
+markdown-table data.csv
+```
+
+**TSV input with right alignment:**
+```bash
+cat data.tsv | markdown-table -d tab -a right
+```
+
+Output:
+```markdown
+|   Name | Age |   City |
