+# ssh-key-gen
+
+Generate SSH key pairs with a simple CLI interface. Wraps `ssh-keygen` with sensible defaults, validation, and helpful output.
+
+## Install
+
+```bash
+go install github.com/TataneSan/ssh-key-gen@latest
+```
+
+Or build from source:
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/ssh-key-gen.git
+cd ssh-key-gen
+go build -o ssh-key-gen .
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```
+ssh-key-gen [options]
+```
+
+### Options
+
+| Flag | Description | Default |
+|------|-------------|---------|
+| `-t` | Key type: `ed25519`, `rsa`, `ecdsa` | `ed25519` |
+| `-b` | Key size in bits | ed25519: fixed, RSA: 3072, ECDSA: 256 |
+| `-c` | Comment for the public key | (none) |
+| `-o` | Output path for private key | `~/.ssh/id_<type>` |
+| `-y` | Overwrite existing key without prompting | `false` |
+| `-show` | Display the public key after generation | `true` |
+
+### Examples
+
+**Generate an ed25519 key (recommended):**
+```bash
+./ssh-key-gen
+```
+
+**Generate an RSA 4096-bit key:**
+```bash
+./ssh-key-gen -t rsa -b 4096
+```
+
+**Generate a key with a comment:**
+```bash
+./ssh-key-gen -t ed25519 -c "user@example.com"
+```
+
+**Generate a key to a custom path:**
+```bash
+./ssh-key-gen -o ./deploy_key
+```
+
+**Overwrite an existing key:**
+```bash
+./ssh-key-gen -y -t ed25519
+```
+
+**ECDSA key:**
+```bash
+./ssh-key-gen -t ecdsa -b 521
+```
+
+### Output
+
+After generation, the tool displays:
+- Private and public key paths
+- File permissions (600 for private, 644 for public)
+- The public key content
+- Key fingerprint
+- Deployment instructions
+
+## Key Types
+
