+# markdown-checklist
+
+A fast CLI tool for managing checklists in Markdown files. List, toggle, check, uncheck, add, and remove checklist items without opening an editor.
+
+## Features
+
+- **List** all checklist items with their status
+- **Toggle** items on/off by number
+- **Check/uncheck** specific items
+- **Add** new items to any Markdown file
+- **Progress** bar showing completion percentage
+- **Clear** all checklist items at once
+- Works with any Markdown file (`- [ ]` and `- [x]` syntax)
+- Preserves surrounding content (headings, paragraphs, etc.)
+
+## Installation
+
+### From source
+
+```bash
+go install github.com/TataneSan/markdown-checklist@latest
+```
+
+### Build manually
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/markdown-checklist.git
+cd markdown-checklist
+go build -o markdown-checklist .
+cp markdown-checklist /usr/local/bin/
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```
+markdown-checklist <command> [arguments]
+```
+
+### Commands
+
+| Command | Description |
+|---|---|
+| `list [file]` | List all checklist items |
+| `progress [file]` | Show completion progress |
+| `toggle <n> [file]` | Toggle item number n |
+| `check <n> [file]` | Check item number n |
+| `uncheck <n> [file]` | Uncheck item number n |
+| `add <text> [file]` | Add a new unchecked item |
+| `clear [file]` | Remove all checklist items |
+
+If no file is specified, `TODO.md` is used by default.
+
+## Examples
+
+```bash
+# List items in a file
+markdown-checklist list TODO.md
+
+# Show progress
+markdown-checklist progress
+
+# Toggle the first item
+markdown-checklist toggle 1 TODO.md
+
+# Check item 3
+markdown-checklist check 3
+
+# Add a new item
+markdown-checklist add "Write unit tests" README.md
+
+# Uncheck item 2
+markdown-checklist uncheck 2
+
+# Clear all checklist items
+markdown-checklist clear TODO.md
+```
+
+### Workflow example
