+# pdf-text-extract
+
+Extract text from PDF files via CLI. Supports page selection, password-protected PDFs, and statistics output.
+
+## Features
+
+- Extract text from any PDF file
+- Select specific pages or page ranges
+- Password-protected PDF support
+- Statistics mode (characters, words per page)
+- Output to file or stdout
+- Plain text mode (no page headers)
+
+## Installation
+
+```bash
+pip install pdf-text-extract
+```
+
+Or install locally:
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/pdf-text-extract.git
+cd pdf-text-extract
+pip install .
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```
+pdf-text-extract <file> [options]
+```
+
+### Options
+
+| Flag | Description |
+|---|---|
+| `-p, --pages` | Page numbers or ranges (e.g., `1 2 3-5`) |
+| `-o, --output` | Output file (default: stdout) |
+| `--password` | Password for encrypted PDFs |
+| `--stats` | Show extraction statistics |
+| `--plain` | Plain text without page headers |
+
+## Examples
+
+```bash
+# Extract all text
+pdf-text-extract document.pdf
+
+# Extract specific pages
+pdf-text-extract document.pdf -p 1 2 3
+
+# Extract page range
+pdf-text-extract document.pdf -p 1-10
+
+# Save to file
+pdf-text-extract document.pdf -o output.txt
+
+# Plain text output (no page headers)
+pdf-text-extract document.pdf --plain
+
+# Show statistics
+pdf-text-extract document.pdf --stats
+# Pages extracted: 5/5
+# Characters: 12345
+# Words: 2345
+#   Page 1: 2500 chars, 480 words
+#   Page 2: 2400 chars, 460 words
+#   ...
+
+# Password-protected PDF
+pdf-text-extract document.pdf --password secret123
+
+# Pipe to other tools
+pdf-text-extract document.pdf --plain | grep -i "important"
+pdf-text-extract document.pdf --plain | wc -w
+```
+
