+# git-merge-conflict-finder
+
+A fast CLI tool written in Go that scans a Git repository for unresolved merge conflict markers and reports the affected files with line numbers.
+
+## Features
+
+- Scans all files in a Git repository for `<<<<<<<`, `=======`, and `>>>>>>>` markers
+- Reports the number of conflicts per file and their exact line ranges
+- JSON output for integration with scripts and CI pipelines
+- Quiet mode that outputs only file paths (one per line)
+- Skips `.git`, `node_modules`, and other common directories by default
+- Exit code 1 when conflicts are found (useful for CI checks)
+
+## Install
+
+```bash
+go install github.com/TataneSan/git-merge-conflict-finder@latest
+```
+
+Or build from source:
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/git-merge-conflict-finder.git
+cd git-merge-conflict-finder
+go build -o git-merge-conflict-finder .
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```
+git-merge-conflict-finder [options] [directory]
+```
+
+### Options
+
+| Flag    | Description                                           |
+|---------|-------------------------------------------------------|
+| `-all`  | Scan all files, including hidden and ignored dirs     |
+| `-quiet`| Only output file paths (one per line)                 |
+| `-json` | Output results in JSON format                         |
+| `-h`    | Show help                                             |
+
+### Examples
+
+Scan the current directory:
+
+```bash
+git-merge-conflict-finder
+```
+
+Scan a specific directory:
+
+```bash
+git-merge-conflict-finder /path/to/repo
+```
+
+JSON output:
+
+```bash
+git-merge-conflict-finder -json .
+```
+
+Quiet mode (file paths only):
+
+```bash
+git-merge-conflict-finder -quiet .
+```
+
+Use in CI to fail the build if conflicts exist:
+
+```bash
+git-merge-conflict-finder ./src || { echo "Merge conflicts found!"; exit 1; }
+```
+
+## Output
+
+### Default (text)
+
