+# docker-compose-validator
+
+A fast CLI tool written in Go that validates docker-compose files for syntax errors, deprecated options, security issues, and best practices.
+
+## Features
+
+- Checks YAML syntax (tabs, indentation)
+- Detects missing required `services` key
+- Flags deprecated fields: `version`, `links`, `volumes_from`, `extends`
+- Security checks: privileged mode, hardcoded secrets
+- Best practices: `latest` tag usage, missing healthchecks, port protocol
+- JSON output for CI/CD integration
+- Exit code 1 when errors are found
+
+## Install
+
+```bash
+go install github.com/TataneSan/docker-compose-validator@latest
+```
+
+Or build from source:
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/docker-compose-validator.git
+cd docker-compose-validator
+go build -o docker-compose-validator .
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```
+docker-compose-validator [options] [file-or-directory]
+```
+
+### Options
+
+| Flag    | Description                                         |
+|---------|-----------------------------------------------------|
+| `-json` | Output results in JSON format                       |
+| `-warn` | Also show warnings (not just errors)                |
+| `-h`    | Show help                                           |
+
+### Examples
+
+Validate the current directory:
+
+```bash
+docker-compose-validator
+```
+
+Validate a specific file:
+
+```bash
+docker-compose-validator /path/to/docker-compose.yml
+```
+
+Show warnings too:
+
+```bash
+docker-compose-validator -warn .
+```
+
+JSON output:
+
+```bash
+docker-compose-validator -json .
+```
+
+Use in CI:
+
+```bash
+docker-compose-validator -warn docker-compose.yml || { echo "Validation failed!"; exit 1; }
+```
+
+## Checks Performed
+
+| Category     | Check                                          | Level   |
+|--------------|-------------------------------------------------|---------|
