+# git-submodule-list
+
+A fast CLI tool written in Go that lists and displays information about Git submodules in a repository.
+
+## Features
+
+- Reads `.gitmodules` and Git tree data
+- Shows path, URL, and commit SHA for each submodule
+- Table, JSON, URL-only, and path-only output modes
+- No external dependencies
+
+## Install
+
+```bash
+go install github.com/TataneSan/git-submodule-list@latest
+```
+
+Or build from source:
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/git-submodule-list.git
+cd git-submodule-list
+go build -o git-submodule-list .
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```
+git-submodule-list [options] [directory]
+```
+
+### Options
+
+| Flag    | Description                        |
+|---------|------------------------------------|
+| `-json` | Output in JSON format              |
+| `-url`  | Show only URLs (one per line)     |
+| `-path` | Show only paths (one per line)    |
+| `-h`    | Show help                          |
+
+### Examples
+
+List submodules in the current repo:
+
+```bash
+git-submodule-list
+```
+
+List submodules in a specific repo:
+
+```bash
+git-submodule-list /path/to/repo
+```
+
+JSON output:
+
+```bash
+git-submodule-list -json .
+```
+
+Get only URLs:
+
+```bash
+git-submodule-list -url .
+```
+
+Get only paths:
+
+```bash
+git-submodule-list -path .
+```
+
+## Output
+
+### Table (default)
+
+```
+PATH                        URL                                     COMMIT
