+# env-to-json
+
+A fast CLI tool written in Go that converts `.env` files to JSON format.
+
+## Features
+
+- Reads standard `.env` file format (KEY=VALUE)
+- Supports comments (`#`), blank lines, and `export` prefix
+- Handles single and double quoted values
+- Pretty-print and compact JSON output
+- Reads from file or stdin
+
+## Install
+
+```bash
+go install github.com/TataneSan/env-to-json@latest
+```
+
+Or build from source:
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/env-to-json.git
+cd env-to-json
+go build -o env-to-json .
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```
+env-to-json [options] [file]
+```
+
+### Options
+
+| Flag       | Description                             |
+|------------|-----------------------------------------|
+| `-compact` | Output compact JSON (single line)       |
+| `-h`       | Show help                               |
+
+### Examples
+
+Convert a .env file:
+
+```bash
+env-to-json .env
+```
+
+Compact output:
+
+```bash
+env-to-json -compact .env
+```
+
+Read from stdin:
+
+```bash
+cat .env | env-to-json
+```
+
+Pipe to jq:
+
+```bash
+env-to-json -compact .env | jq '.DB_HOST'
+```
+
+## Input Format
+
+```
+# Comments are ignored
+DB_HOST=localhost
+DB_PORT=5432
+DB_NAME="myapp"
+DB_PASSWORD='secret'
+export API_KEY=abc123
+EMPTY_VAL=
+```
+
+## Output
