+# path-join
+
+A comprehensive file path manipulation tool for the command line.
+
+Provides common path operations like join, dirname, basename, and more in a single lightweight CLI tool.
+
+## Install
+
+```bash
+go install github.com/TataneSan/path-join@latest
+```
+
+Or build from source:
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/path-join.git
+cd path-join
+go build -o path-join .
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```
+path-join <command> [arguments]
+```
+
+## Commands
+
+| Command              | Description                    |
+|----------------------|--------------------------------|
+| `join`               | Join path elements             |
+| `dirname`            | Get directory portion          |
+| `basename`           | Get base name                  |
+| `ext`                | Get file extension             |
+| `abs`                | Get absolute path              |
+| `clean`              | Clean up path                  |
+| `rel`                | Get relative path              |
+| `exists`             | Check if path exists           |
+| `isabs`              | Check if path is absolute      |
+| `homedir`            | Print home directory           |
+| `split`              | Split path into components     |
+| `walk`               | Walk directory tree            |
+
+## Examples
+
+Join path elements:
+```bash
+path-join join /usr local/bin
+# Output: /usr/local/bin
+```
+
+Get directory portion:
+```bash
+path-join dirname /usr/local/bin
+# Output: /usr/local
+```
+
+Get base name:
+```bash
+path-join basename /usr/local/file.txt
+# Output: file.txt
+```
+
+Get absolute path:
+```bash
+path-join abs ./config
+# Output: /home/user/project/config
+```
+
+Get relative path:
+```bash
+path-join rel /usr/local /usr/local/bin
+# Output: bin
+```
+
+Split path into components:
+```bash
+path-join split /usr/local/file.txt
