+# cors-proxy
+
+A lightweight CORS proxy written in Go that forwards HTTP requests to target URLs while adding appropriate CORS headers to the responses. Useful for development and for bypassing CORS restrictions when calling APIs from the browser.
+
+## Features
+
+- Forward any HTTP request (GET, POST, PUT, DELETE, PATCH, HEAD)
+- Full CORS header support (preflight/OPTIONS handling)
+- Configurable listen port, host, allowed origin, and timeout
+- Health check endpoint (`/health`)
+- Request logging
+- Graceful shutdown on SIGINT/SIGTERM
+- Single binary, no external dependencies
+
+## Installation
+
+### From source
+
+```bash
+go install github.com/TataneSan/cors-proxy@latest
+```
+
+### Build manually
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/cors-proxy.git
+cd cors-proxy
+go build -o cors-proxy .
+```
+
+### Docker
+
+```bash
+docker build -t cors-proxy .
+docker run -p 8080:8080 cors-proxy
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+### Basic
+
+```bash
+./cors-proxy
+```
+
+Starts the proxy on `http://127.0.0.1:8080`.
+
+### Flags
+
+```
+  -port int
+        Port to listen on (default 8080)
+  -host string
+        Host to bind to (default "127.0.0.1")
+  -allow-origin string
+        Allowed origin for CORS (default "*")
+  -timeout int
+        Request timeout in seconds (default 30)
+```
+
+### Examples
+
+```bash
+# Listen on all interfaces on port 3000
+./cors-proxy -port 3000 -host 0.0.0.0
+
+# Restrict CORS to a specific origin
+./cors-proxy -allow-origin https://myapp.local
+
+# Increase timeout to 60 seconds
+./cors-proxy -timeout 60
+```
+
+### Proxy requests
+
+Once the proxy is running, prepend `/proxy?url=` to any target URL:
+
+```bash
