+# timestamp-api
+
+A lightweight REST API that returns the current timestamp in various formats. Useful for testing, debugging, and synchronizing clocks across systems.
+
+## Features
+
+- Multiple timestamp formats: Unix, ISO 8601, RFC 3339, human-readable
+- Unix timestamp converter (seconds, milliseconds, nanoseconds auto-detection)
+- Configurable host and port
+- Health check endpoint
+- Single binary, zero dependencies
+
+## Installation
+
+### From source
+
+```bash
+go install github.com/TataneSan/timestamp-api@latest
+```
+
+### Build manually
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/timestamp-api.git
+cd timestamp-api
+go build -o timestamp-api .
+```
+
+### Docker
+
+```bash
+docker build -t timestamp-api .
+docker run -p 8080:8080 timestamp-api
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+### Start the server
+
+```bash
+./timestamp-api
+```
+
+Starts on `http://127.0.0.1:8080`.
+
+### Flags
+
+```
+  -port int     Port to listen on (default 8080)
+  -host string  Host to bind to (default "127.0.0.1")
+```
+
+### Examples
+
+```bash
+# Listen on all interfaces
+./timestamp-api -host 0.0.0.0 -port 3000
+```
+
+### Endpoints
+
+| Endpoint | Description | Response Type |
+|---|---|---|
+| `GET /` | All timestamp formats | JSON |
+| `GET /now` | All timestamp formats (alias) | JSON |
+| `GET /unix` | Unix epoch seconds | text |
+| `GET /unix-millis` | Unix epoch milliseconds | text |
+| `GET /unix-nano` | Unix epoch nanoseconds | text |
+| `GET /iso` | ISO 8601 date-time | text |
+| `GET /rfc3339` | RFC 3339 date-time | text |
+| `GET /date` | Date (YYYY-MM-DD) | text |
+| `GET /time` | Time (HH:MM:SS) | text |
+| `GET /datetime` | Date and time | text |
+| `GET /convert?unix=1234567890` | Convert Unix timestamp | JSON |
+| `GET /health` | Health check | JSON |
+
+### Example responses
+
