+# Env Docs
+
+CLI tool that generates Markdown documentation from `.env` files. Parses comments for metadata like type, default values, and requirements.
+
+## Features
+
+- Parse `.env` files and extract variables
+- Read metadata from comments (required, type, default, example)
+- Generate a Markdown table + detailed section
+- Output to file or stdout
+- Single binary, zero dependencies
+
+## Install
+
+```bash
+go install github.com/TataneSan/env-docs@latest
+# or
+go build -o env-docs .
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```
+env-docs [OPTIONS] [FILE]
+```
+
+### Options
+
+| Flag | Description | Default |
+|------|-------------|---------|
+| `-o, --output FILE` | Output file | stdout |
+| `-h, --help` | Show help | |
+
+### Comment Metadata
+
+Add these comments above a variable in your `.env`:
+
+```
+# Database host
+# required
+# type: string
+DB_HOST=localhost
+
+# API port
+# type: int
+# default: 3000
+API_PORT=3000
+
+# API key
+# required
+# type: string
+# example: sk-abc123
+API_KEY=
+```
+
+### Examples
+
+Generate docs from `.env` in current directory:
+```bash
+env-docs
+```
+
+Output to a specific file:
+```bash
+env-docs .env.example -o ENV.md
+```
+
+Use a custom .env path:
+```bash
+env-docs --output docs/env-vars.md config/.env.production
+```
+
+## Output Format
+
+The generated Markdown includes:
+1. Summary table (variable, description, required, type, default)
+2. Detailed section per variable with all metadata
+
