+# crontab-lint
+
+Validate and lint crontab files from the command line.
+
+## Features
+
+- Validates field ranges (minute, hour, day-of-month, month, day-of-week)
+- Warns about every-minute jobs (`* * * * *`)
+- Detects when both day-of-month and day-of-week are set (cron OR logic)
+- Flags commands without absolute paths
+- Notes missing output redirection
+- Colorized output (error / warning / info)
+- Reads from a file or stdin
+- Exit code 0 on clean, 1 on errors/warnings
+
+## Install
+
+```bash
+go install github.com/TataneSan/crontab-lint@latest
+```
+
+Or build from source:
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/crontab-lint.git
+cd crontab-lint
+go build -o crontab-lint .
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```bash
+# Lint a file
+crontab-lint /etc/crontab
+
+# Lint from stdin
+crontab-lint < my-crontab.txt
+
+# Pipe crontab output
+crontab -l | crontab-lint
+```
+
+## Example
+
+```bash
+$ cat my-crontab
+# Backup every day at 2am
+0 2 * * * backup.sh
+# Run every minute (warning)
+* * * * * check_health
+# Invalid minute
+60 * * * * /usr/bin/cleanup > /dev/null
+# Both day fields set
+0 0 15 * 5 /usr/bin/report.sh >> /var/log/report.log
+
+$ crontab-lint my-crontab
+[warning] L2: command "backup.sh" may not be in PATH — consider using an absolute path
+    0 2 * * * backup.sh
+[info] L2: no output redirection — cron will email output to the user
+    0 2 * * * backup.sh
+[warning] L4: runs every minute — verify this is intentional
+    * * * * * check_health
+[info] L4: no output redirection — cron will email output to the user
+    * * * * * check_health
+[error] L6: invalid minute field: "60"
+    60 * * * * /usr/bin/cleanup > /dev/null
+[warning] L8: both day-of-month and day-of-week are restricted — cron uses OR logic, not AND
+    0 0 15 * 5 /usr/bin/report.sh >> /var/log/report.log
+
+1 error(s), 3 warning(s), 2 info(s)
+```
+
+## Exit Codes
+
+| Code | Meaning |
+|------|---------|
+| 0    | No errors or warnings |
+| 1    | Errors or warnings found |
