+# cli-contacts
+
+Simple command-line address book with JSON persistence.
+
+## Features
+
+- Add, list, get, edit, and delete contacts
+- Search contacts by name, phone, email, or notes
+- Interactive mode for adding contacts
+- Import/export contacts as JSON
+- Data stored in `~/.cli-contacts/contacts.json`
+
+## Install
+
+```bash
+go install github.com/TataneSan/cli-contacts@latest
+```
+
+Or build from source:
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/cli-contacts.git
+cd cli-contacts
+go build -o cli-contacts .
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```bash
+# Add a contact
+cli-contacts add "Alice Dupont" --phone "+33612345678" --email "alice@example.com"
+
+# List all contacts
+cli-contacts list
+
+# Search contacts
+cli-contacts list alice
+
+# Get a contact by ID
+cli-contacts get 1
+
+# Edit a contact
+cli-contacts edit 1 --phone "+33698765432" --email "new@example.com"
+
+# Delete a contact
+cli-contacts delete 1
+
+# Add interactively
+cli-contacts new
+
+# Export contacts
+cli-contacts export backup.json
+
+# Import contacts
+cli-contacts import backup.json
+```
+
+## Example
+
+```bash
+$ cli-contacts add "Alice" --phone "+33612345678" --email "alice@example.com"
+Added contact #1: Alice
+
+$ cli-contacts add "Bob" --phone "+33698765432"
+Added contact #2: Bob
+
+$ cli-contacts list
+  ID    Name                 Phone           Email
+  ---------------------------------------------------------------
+  1     Alice                +33612345678    alice@example.com
+  2     Bob                  +33698765432
+
+  2 contact(s)
+
+$ cli-contacts get 1
+  ID:    1
+  Name:  Alice
+  Phone: +33612345678
