+# csv-split
+
+Split large CSV files into smaller, manageable chunks. Preserves headers in each output file.
+
+## Install
+
+```bash
+go install github.com/TataneSan/csv-split@latest
+```
+
+Or build from source:
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/csv-split.git
+cd csv-split
+go build -o csv-split .
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```
+csv-split -n <count> <file.csv>          Split into N files
+csv-split -l <lines> <file.csv>           Split by lines per file
+```
+
+## Options
+
+| Flag | Description | Default |
+|------|-------------|---------|
+| `-n` | Number of output files | — |
+| `-l` | Lines per output file (including header) | — |
+| `-o` | Output directory | Same dir as input |
+| `-p` | Output filename prefix | Input filename |
+| `-d` | CSV delimiter | Comma (`,`) |
+| `-h` | Show help message | — |
+
+## Examples
+
+Split into 10 roughly equal files:
+```bash
+csv-split -n 10 large.csv
+```
+
+Split into files of 10,000 lines each:
+```bash
+csv-split -l 10000 large.csv
+```
+
+Custom output directory and prefix:
+```bash
+csv-split -n 5 -o ./output -p part large.csv
+```
+
+Split a semicolon-delimited file:
+```bash
+csv-split -d ';' -n 3 data.csv
+```
+
+## Features
+
+- Split by number of files or lines per file
+- Header row preserved in every output file
+- Configurable delimiter (comma, semicolon, tab, etc.)
+- Variable number of fields supported
+- Sequential numbered output files (`prefix_0001.csv`, `prefix_0002.csv`, ...)
+- Summary report with row counts
+
+## License
+
+MIT
