+# env-to-toml
+
+Convert .env files to TOML format with automatic type detection.
+
+## Install
+
+```bash
+go install github.com/TataneSan/env-to-toml@latest
+```
+
+Or build from source:
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/env-to-toml.git
+cd env-to-toml
+go build -o env-to-toml .
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```
+env-to-toml <file.env>              Convert and print to stdout
+env-to-toml <file.env> -o out.toml  Convert and write to file
+cat .env | env-to-toml              Convert from stdin
+```
+
+## Options
+
+| Flag | Description | Default |
+|------|-------------|---------|
+| `-o` | Output file | stdout |
+| `-s` | Sort keys alphabetically | true |
+| `-h` | Show help message | — |
+
+## Examples
+
+Convert and print to stdout:
+```bash
+env-to-toml .env
+```
+
+Convert and write to file:
+```bash
+env-to-toml .env -o config.toml
+```
+
+Convert from stdin:
+```bash
+cat .env.example | env-to-toml > config.toml
+```
+
+## Input
+
+```env
+DB_HOST=localhost
+DB_PORT=5432
+APP_NAME="MyApp"
+DEBUG=true
+RATE=3.14
+```
+
+## Output
+
+```toml
+app_name = "MyApp"
+db_host = "localhost"
+db_port = 5432
+debug = true
+rate = 3.14
+```
+
+## Features
+
+- Automatic type detection (string, int, float, bool)
+- Nested tables via double underscore (`APP__DB__HOST` -> `[app.db] host`)
+- Sorted keys for consistent output
+- Handles quoted and unquoted values
+- Stdin support for piping
