+# batch-api
+
+Execute multiple HTTP requests in parallel and get all responses at once.
+
+Accepts a list of HTTP requests, executes them concurrently, and returns all responses with status codes, headers, bodies, and timing information.
+
+## Features
+
+- **Parallel execution** — Execute up to 100 requests concurrently (10 at a time)
+- **Any HTTP method** — GET, POST, PUT, DELETE, PATCH, etc.
+- **Custom headers** — Set arbitrary headers per request
+- **Request body support** — Send JSON or any body content
+- **Timing info** — Duration in milliseconds per request
+- **Response details** — Status code, headers, and body for each response
+- **Single request mode** — Proxy a single request via `/single`
+- **Debug endpoint** — Inspect incoming requests with `/debug`
+
+## Endpoints
+
+| Method | Path | Description |
+|--------|------|-------------|
+| POST | `/batch` | Execute multiple HTTP requests in parallel |
+| POST | `/single` | Execute a single HTTP request |
+| GET | `/debug` | Debug endpoint — returns request details |
+| GET | `/health` | Health check |
+
+## Install
+
+```bash
+go install github.com/TataneSan/batch-api@latest
+```
+
+Or build manually:
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/batch-api.git
+cd batch-api
+go build -o batch-api .
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```bash
+# Start the server (defaults to port 8080)
+./batch-api
+```
+
+### Batch request
+
+```bash
+curl -X POST http://localhost:8080/batch \
+  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
+  -d '{
+    "requests": [
+      {
+        "id": "google",
+        "method": "GET",
+        "url": "https://httpbin.org/get"
+      },
+      {
+        "id": "post-test",
+        "method": "POST",
+        "url": "https://httpbin.org/post",
+        "header": {"X-Custom": "test"},
+        "body": "{\"key\": \"value\"}"
+      },
+      {
+        "id": "status-check",
+        "method": "GET",
+        "url": "https://httpbin.org/status/404"
+      }
+    ]
+  }'
+```
+
+Response:
+```json
+{
