+# transform-api
+
+REST API for transforming JSON data with operations like map, filter, sort, group, flatten, and unique. Send your data with a transformation instruction and get back the result.
+
+## Features
+
+- **map** — Transform each item in an array
+- **filter** — Filter array items by a condition
+- **sort** — Sort array by a key (ascending or descending)
+- **group** — Group array items by a key
+- **flatten** — Flatten nested arrays into a single array
+- **unique** — Remove duplicate items by a key
+- **limit** — Paginate results with offset and limit
+- Dot-notation path support for nested data
+
+## Installation
+
+```bash
+go install github.com/TataneSan/transform-api@latest
+```
+
+Or build from source:
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/transform-api.git
+cd transform-api
+go build -o transform-api .
+./transform-api
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+Start the server:
+
+```bash
+./transform-api
+# Listening on :8080
+```
+
+### API Endpoint
+
+**POST** `/transform`
+
+#### Sort Example
+
+```bash
+curl -sX POST http://localhost:8080/transform \
+  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
+  -d '{
+    "data": [
+      {"name": "Charlie", "age": 30},
+      {"name": "Alice", "age": 25},
+      {"name": "Bob", "age": 35}
+    ],
+    "operation": "sort",
+    "key": "name"
+  }' | jq .
+```
+
+Response:
+```json
+{
+  "data": [
+    {"name": "Alice", "age": 25},
+    {"name": "Bob", "age": 35},
+    {"name": "Charlie", "age": 30}
+  ],
+  "count": 3,
+  "operation": "sort"
+}
+```
+
+#### Filter Example
+
+```bash
+curl -sX POST http://localhost:8080/transform \
+  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
+  -d '{
