+# merge-api
+
+REST API for merging JSON data with multiple strategies. Combine two JSON objects or arrays using deep merge, shallow merge, array append, or array replace.
+
+## Features
+
+- **deep** — Recursively merge nested objects and concatenate arrays (default)
+- **shallow** — Merge top-level keys only, override wins
+- **array-append** — Append override array to base array
+- **array-replace** — Replace base array with override array
+- Configurable merge strategy per request
+
+## Installation
+
+```bash
+go install github.com/TataneSan/merge-api@latest
+```
+
+Or build from source:
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/merge-api.git
+cd merge-api
+go build -o merge-api .
+./merge-api
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+Start the server:
+
+```bash
+./merge-api
+# Listening on :8080
+```
+
+### API Endpoint
+
+**POST** `/merge`
+
+#### Deep Merge Example
+
+```bash
+curl -sX POST http://localhost:8080/merge \
+  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
+  -d '{
+    "base": {
+      "name": "app",
+      "config": {
+        "debug": false,
+        "port": 3000,
+        "features": ["auth"]
+      }
+    },
+    "override": {
+      "config": {
+        "debug": true,
+        "host": "0.0.0.0",
+        "features": ["logging"]
+      },
+      "version": "1.0"
+    },
+    "strategy": "deep"
+  }' | jq .
+```
+
+Response:
+```json
+{
+  "merged": {
+    "name": "app",
+    "config": {
+      "debug": true,
+      "port": 3000,
+      "host": "0.0.0.0",
+      "features": ["auth", "logging"]
+    },
+    "version": "1.0"
