+# log-sampler
+
+Sample log files for analysis. Extract a random subset of lines by percentage or count — useful for analyzing massive log files without processing every line.
+
+## Features
+
+- Sample by percentage (e.g., 1%, 10%, 50%)
+- Sample by exact count (e.g., 100 lines)
+- Reproducible results with `--seed`
+- Reads from file or stdin (pipe-friendly)
+- Large file support with buffered scanning
+- Streaming percentage mode (no full file load needed)
+
+## Installation
+
+```bash
+go install github.com/TataneSan/log-sampler@latest
+```
+
+Or build from source:
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/log-sampler.git
+cd log-sampler
+go build -o log-sampler .
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```bash
+log-sampler [options] [file]
+```
+
+### Options
+
+| Flag | Description |
+|---|---|
+| `-p, --percent FLOAT` | Sample by percentage (0.01 to 100) |
+| `-n, --count INT` | Sample exactly N random lines |
+| `-s, --seed INT` | Random seed for reproducible results |
+| `-h, --help` | Show help |
+
+### Examples
+
+**Sample 10% of a log file (default):**
+
+```bash
+./log-sampler access.log
+# or explicitly:
+./log-sampler -p 10 access.log
+```
+
+**Sample 1% of a large log:**
+
+```bash
+./log-sampler -p 1 production.log
+```
+
+**Sample exactly 100 random lines:**
+
+```bash
+./log-sampler -n 100 access.log
+```
+
+**Reproducible sampling (same seed = same results):**
+
+```bash
+./log-sampler -p 50 -s 42 access.log
+```
+
+**Pipe from another command:**
+
+```bash
+cat huge.log | log-sampler -p 5
+zcat app.log.gz | log-sampler -n 50
+grep "ERROR" app.log | log-sampler -p 20
+```
+
