+# env-to-yaml
+
+Convert `.env` files to YAML format. Parse environment variable files and output clean YAML configuration.
+
+## Features
+
+- Converts `KEY=VALUE` pairs to `key: value` YAML format
+- Handles quoted values (single and double quotes)
+- Properly escapes YAML special characters
+- Preserves comments from .env files
+- Reads from file or stdin (pipe-friendly)
+- Output to file or stdout
+
+## Installation
+
+```bash
+go install github.com/TataneSan/env-to-yaml@latest
+```
+
+Or build from source:
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/env-to-yaml.git
+cd env-to-yaml
+go build -o env-to-yaml .
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```bash
+env-to-yaml [options] [file]
+```
+
+### Options
+
+| Flag | Description |
+|---|---|
+| `-o, --output FILE` | Write output to file instead of stdout |
+| `-h, --help` | Show help |
+
+### Examples
+
+**Convert a .env file:**
+
+```bash
+./env-to-yaml .env
+```
+
+Given `.env`:
+```
+DATABASE_URL=postgres://localhost:5432/mydb
+API_KEY="sk-123456789"
+DEBUG=true
+PORT=3000
+APP_NAME='My App'
+```
+
+Output:
+```yaml
+DATABASE_URL: postgres://localhost:5432/mydb
+API_KEY: sk-123456789
+DEBUG: 'true'
+PORT: '3000'
+APP_NAME: My App
+```
+
+**Output to file:**
+
+```bash
+./env-to-yaml .env -o config.yaml
+```
+
+**Pipe from stdin:**
+
+```bash
+cat .env.production | env-to-yaml > production.yaml
+```
+
