+# docker-rename
+
+A CLI tool to rename Docker containers, with support for batch renaming via interactive mode.
+
+## Install
+
+```bash
+go install github.com/TataneSan/docker-rename@latest
+```
+
+Or build from source:
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/docker-rename.git
+cd docker-rename
+go build -o docker-rename .
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```
+docker-rename list               List all containers with their names
+docker-rename rename <old> <new> Rename a single container
+docker-rename batch              Interactive batch rename mode
+```
+
+### List containers
+
+```bash
+docker-rename list
+```
+
+Shows all containers (running and stopped) with their IDs and status.
+
+### Rename a single container
+
+```bash
+docker-rename rename old-name new-name
+```
+
+Note: The container must be stopped before renaming.
+
+### Batch rename (interactive)
+
+```bash
+docker-rename batch
+```
+
+Interactively renames containers one by one. Press Enter to keep the current name.
+
+## Examples
+
+```bash
+$ docker-rename list
+
+============================================================
+  Docker Containers
+============================================================
+
+  [ 1] web-server                         running (a1b2c3d4e5f6)
+  [ 2] db_postgres_1                      stopped (f6e5d4c3b2a1)
+  [ 3] old-redis                          stopped (1a2b3c4d5e6f)
+
+  Total: 3 containers
+
+$ docker-rename rename old-redis cache-redis
+Renamed: old-redis -> cache-redis
+```
+
+## Requirements
+
+- Docker Engine installed and accessible
+- Permission to run `docker` commands
+
+## License
+
+MIT
