+# cli-dice
+
+Terminal dice roller with standard D&D dice notation.
+
+Roll d4, d6, d8, d10, d12, d20, or any number of sides (2-100).
+Supports multiple dice, modifiers, and seed-based reproducibility.
+
+## Features
+
+- Standard dice notation: `d20`, `2d6`, `4d10+5`
+- Multiple dice in a single roll: `d8 d12`
+- Bonuses and penalties: `3d6+2`, `d20-1`
+- Seed support for reproducible rolls: `-s 42`
+- Quiet mode for scripting: `-q`
+- Single binary, no dependencies
+
+## Install
+
+### From source
+
+```bash
+go install github.com/TataneSan/cli-dice@latest
+```
+
+### Build manually
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/cli-dice.git
+cd cli-dice
+go build -o cli-dice .
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```
+cli-dice [options] [dice]
+```
+
+### Dice notation
+
+| Input | Description |
+|-------|-------------|
+| `d20` | Roll one d20 |
+| `2d6` | Roll two d6 |
+| `4d10+5` | Roll four d10 and add 5 |
+| `d8-2` | Roll one d8 and subtract 2 |
+| `d8 d12` | Roll one d8 and one d12 |
+
+### Options
+
+| Flag | Description |
+|------|-------------|
+| `-h, --help` | Show help message |
+| `-v, --version` | Show version |
+| `-s, --seed N` | Set random seed for reproducible rolls |
+| `-q, --quiet` | Only print the final result number |
+
+### Examples
+
+```bash
+# Roll one d20 (default if no args)
+$ cli-dice d20
+[17] = 17
+
+# Roll two d6
+$ cli-dice 2d6
+[3,5] = 8
+
+# Roll four d10 with +5 bonus
+$ cli-dice 4d10+5
+[7,3,1,6] +5 = 22
+
+# Roll multiple different dice
+$ cli-dice d8 d12
+[1] = 1
+[9] = 9
+Total: 10
+
