+# json-rename-keys
+
+Recursively rename keys in JSON files from the command line. Supports exact matching and regex patterns.
+
+## Install
+
+```bash
+go install github.com/TataneSan/json-rename-keys@latest
+```
+
+Or build from source:
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/json-rename-keys.git
+cd json-rename-keys
+go build -o json-rename-keys .
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```
+json-rename-keys [OPTIONS] <input> <old1=new1> [old2=new2 ...]
+```
+
+### Options
+
+| Flag | Description |
+|------|-------------|
+| `-o, --output FILE` | Write output to file instead of stdout |
+| `-i, --inplace` | Modify the input file in place |
+| `-c, --compact` | Compact output (no indentation) |
+| `-h, --help` | Show help message |
+
+### Arguments
+
+- **input** — Path to a JSON file, or `-` to read from stdin
+- **old=new** — One or more key rename mappings
+
+## Examples
+
+### Rename specific keys
+
+```bash
+json-rename-keys data.json name=fullName age=userAge
+```
+
+Input:
+```json
+{"name": "Alice", "age": 30}
+```
+
+Output:
+```json
+{
+  "fullName": "Alice",
+  "userAge": 30
+}
+```
+
+### In-place modification
+
+```bash
+json-rename-keys -i data.json firstName=name lastName=surname
+```
+
+### Pipe from stdin
+
+```bash
+cat data.json | json-rename-keys - id=userId name=displayName
+```
+
+### Regex-based renaming
+
+Prefix a key with `re:` to use regex matching:
+
+```bash
+json-rename-keys data.json 're:^user_=usr_'
+```
