+# csv-statistics
+
+Compute basic statistics for each column in a CSV file.
+
+## Install
+
+```bash
+go install github.com/TataneSan/csv-statistics@latest
+```
+
+Or build from source:
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/csv-statistics.git
+cd csv-statistics
+go build -o csv-statistics .
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```
+csv-statistics [OPTIONS] <file>
+```
+
+### Options
+
+| Flag | Description |
+|------|-------------|
+| `-d, --delimiter R` | Delimiter character (default: auto-detect) |
+| `-h, --help` | Show help message |
+
+## Examples
+
+```bash
+csv-statistics data.csv
+csv-statistics -d ';' data.csv
+```
+
+### Output
+
+For each column, displays:
+- Non-empty / empty count
+- Unique values count
+- Numeric statistics (if column is numeric): min, max, sum, mean, median, standard deviation
+- Top 5 most common values
+
+Example output:
+```
+CSV Statistics — 100 rows, 4 columns
+
+Column: age
+  Non-empty: 98 / 100
+  Empty:     2
+  Unique:    35
+  --- Numeric ---
+  Min:     18.0
+  Max:     65.0
+  Sum:     3245.0
+  Mean:    33.11
+  Median:  32.0
+  StdDev:  11.23
+  Top values:
+    25                                       8
+    30                                       7
+    35                                       6
+    28                                       5
+    40                                       4
+```
+
+## Features
+
+- Auto-detects CSV delimiters (comma, semicolon, tab, pipe)
+- Automatic numeric column detection
+- Comprehensive statistics: min, max, sum, mean, median, standard deviation
+- Top value frequency analysis
+- Handles empty values and irregular row lengths
+
+## License
