+# dedup-lines
+
+CLI tool to remove duplicate lines from files. Supports stdin piping, sorted output, case-insensitive comparison, and statistics.
+
+## Install
+
+```bash
+go install github.com/TataneSan/dedup-lines@latest
+```
+
+Or build from source:
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/dedup-lines.git
+cd dedup-lines
+go build -o dedup-lines .
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```
+dedup-lines [options] [files...]
+cat file.txt | dedup-lines
+```
+
+### Options
+
+| Flag | Description |
+|------|-------------|
+| `-s, --sort` | Sort output alphabetically |
+| `-i, --ignore-case` | Case-insensitive comparison |
+| `-c, --count` | Show duplicate statistics only |
+| `-h, --help` | Show help message |
+
+## Examples
+
+Remove duplicates from a file (creates `words.txt.dedup`):
+
+```bash
+dedup-lines words.txt
+```
+
+Pipe through stdin:
+
+```bash
+cat data.txt | dedup-lines
+```
+
+Sorted, case-insensitive output:
+
+```bash
+dedup-lines -s -i file.txt
+```
+
+Show statistics without modifying files:
+
+```bash
+dedup-lines -c file.txt
+# File: file.txt
+# Total lines: 150
+# Unique lines: 120
+# Duplicates: 30
+```
+
+Process multiple files:
+
+```bash
+dedup-lines -s file1.txt file2.txt file3.txt
+```
+
