+# json-subset
+
+CLI tool to extract a subset of keys from JSON data. Supports recursive filtering, inverted selection, and pretty-printing.
+
+## Install
+
+```bash
+go install github.com/TataneSan/json-subset@latest
+```
+
+Or build from source:
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/json-subset.git
+cd json-subset
+go build -o json-subset .
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```
+json-subset [options] key1 key2 key3
+cat data.json | json-subset key1 key2
+json-subset -f data.json key1 key2
+```
+
+### Options
+
+| Flag | Description |
+|------|-------------|
+| `-f, --file FILE` | Read JSON from FILE (default: stdin) |
+| `-o, --output FILE` | Write output to FILE (default: stdout) |
+| `-p, --pretty` | Pretty-print output with indentation |
+| `-i, --invert` | Invert selection (exclude specified keys) |
+| `-h, --help` | Show help message |
+
+## Examples
+
+Extract specific keys:
+
+```bash
+cat data.json | json-subset name email
+```
+
+Pretty-print output:
+
+```bash
+json-subset -f config.json -p host port
+```
+
+Exclude keys (invert selection):
+
+```bash
+json-subset -f data.json -i password secret
+```
+
+Write to file:
+
+```bash
+json-subset -f data.json -p -o out.json id name
+```
+
+## Recursive Filtering
+
+The tool recursively filters keys in nested objects. Arrays are traversed and objects within them are also filtered.
+
+```bash
+echo '{"users":[{"name":"Alice","age":30},{"name":"Bob","age":25}]}' | json-subset -p users
+```
+
+Output:
+
+```json
+{
+  "users": [
+    {"name": "Alice"},
+    {"name": "Bob"}
+  ]
