+# env-sanitize
+
+CLI tool to sanitize .env files by replacing sensitive values with `****` placeholders. Useful for safely sharing environment files or including them in version control.
+
+## Install
+
+```bash
+go install github.com/TataneSan/env-sanitize@latest
+```
+
+Or build from source:
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/env-sanitize.git
+cd env-sanitize
+go build -o env-sanitize .
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```
+env-sanitize [options] [file.env]
+cat .env | env-sanitize
+```
+
+### Options
+
+| Flag | Description |
+|------|-------------|
+| `-f, --file FILE` | Read from FILE (default: stdin) |
+| `-o, --output FILE` | Write sanitized output to FILE |
+| `-l, --list` | List sensitive keys found |
+| `-s, --show` | Show only sanitized lines |
+| `-p, --pattern PAT` | Add custom pattern (repeatable) |
+| `-h, --help` | Show help message |
+
+## Built-in Patterns
+
+The tool automatically detects keys containing:
+- `password`, `passwd`, `pwd`
+- `secret`, `private_key`
+- `token`, `auth_token`, `access_token`
+- `api_key`, `secret_key`
+- `credential`
+
+## Examples
+
+Sanitize a file and write to a new file:
+
+```bash
+env-sanitize -f .env -o .env.safe
+```
+
+List sensitive keys:
+
+```bash
+env-sanitize -l -f .env
+# [password    ] DB_PASSWORD
+# [key         ] API_KEY
+# [secret      ] SECRET_TOKEN
+# 3 sensitive key(s) found.
+```
+
+Add custom patterns:
+
+```bash
+env-sanitize -f .env -p webhook -p license
+```
+
+Pipe from stdin:
+
+```bash
+cat .env | env-sanitize
+```
+
+Show only sensitive lines:
+
+```bash
