+# dir-compare
+
+CLI tool to compare the contents of two directories. Supports hash-based comparison and directory ignoring.
+
+## Install
+
+```bash
+go install github.com/TataneSan/dir-compare@latest
+```
+
+Or build from source:
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/dir-compare.git
+cd dir-compare
+go build -o dir-compare .
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```
+dir-compare [options] DIR1 DIR2
+```
+
+### Options
+
+| Flag | Description |
+|------|-------------|
+| `-s, --summary` | Show summary only (no file list) |
+| `--hash` | Compare files by SHA-256 hash instead of size |
+| `-I, --ignore D` | Ignore directory D (repeatable) |
+| `-h, --help` | Show help message |
+
+### Output Symbols
+
+| Symbol | Meaning |
+|--------|---------|
+| `+` | Only in DIR1 |
+| `-` | Only in DIR2 |
+| `~` | Modified (different content) |
+| `!` | Size changed |
+
+## Examples
+
+Basic comparison:
+
+```bash
+dir-compare ./prod ./backup
+```
+
+Summary only:
+
+```bash
+dir-compare -s ./dir1 ./dir2
+```
+
+Hash-based comparison (detects content changes):
+
+```bash
+dir-compare --hash ./src ./dist
+```
+
+Ignore directories:
+
+```bash
+dir-compare -I node_modules -I .git ./a ./b
+```
+
+## License
+
+MIT
