+# glob-match
+
+Test if file paths match a glob pattern from the command line.
+
+## Features
+
+- Supports standard glob patterns: `*`, `?`, `[abc]`, `[!abc]`
+- Supports recursive `**` patterns for deep directory matching
+- Read paths from arguments or stdin
+- Exit code 0 if all match, 1 if any don't match
+- Single binary, no dependencies
+
+## Install
+
+```bash
+go install github.com/TataneSan/glob-match@latest
+```
+
+Or build from source:
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/glob-match.git
+cd glob-match
+go build -o glob-match .
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```bash
+glob-match <pattern> <path> [path...]
+```
+
+Reads paths from stdin if none provided as arguments.
+
+### Examples
+
+Match Go files:
+```bash
+glob-match '*.go' main.go test.go README.md
+```
+
+Recursive pattern matching:
+```bash
+glob-match 'src/**/*_test.go' src/pkg/handler_test.go src/main.go
+```
+
+From stdin:
+```bash
+echo -e 'a.go\nb.txt' | glob-match '*.go'
+```
+
+Question mark (single character):
+```bash
+glob-match '?.txt' a.txt abc.txt
+```
+
+Character classes:
+```bash
+glob-match '[ab].go' a.go b.go c.go
+```
+
+## Patterns
+
+| Pattern  | Description                              |
+|----------|------------------------------------------|
+| `*`      | Matches any sequence of non-`/` chars    |
+| `**`     | Matches any chars including `/`          |
+| `?`      | Matches any single non-`/` char          |
+| `[abc]`  | Matches any character in the set         |
+| `[!abc]` | Matches any character not in the set     |
+
+## Exit Codes
+
+| Code | Meaning                              |
+|------|--------------------------------------|
+| 0    | All paths match the pattern          |
+| 1    | Some or none of the paths match      |
+| 2    | Invalid pattern or read error        |
