+# json-group-by
+
+Group JSON array objects by a key from the command line.
+
+## Features
+
+- Group JSON objects by any key
+- Read from file or stdin
+- Sorted output by group key
+- Objects without the key go to `<null>` group
+- Single binary, no dependencies
+
+## Install
+
+```bash
+go install github.com/TataneSan/json-group-by@latest
+```
+
+Or build from source:
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/json-group-by.git
+cd json-group-by
+go build -o json-group-by .
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```bash
+json-group-by <key> [file.json]
+```
+
+Reads JSON from stdin if no file provided.
+
+### Examples
+
+Group by category:
+```bash
+json-group-by category items.json
+```
+
+From stdin:
+```bash
+cat items.json | json-group-by status
+```
+
+With curl:
+```bash
+curl -s https://api.example.com/items | json-group-by type
+```
+
+### Input
+
+```json
+[
+  {"name": "apple", "color": "red"},
+  {"name": "banana", "color": "yellow"},
+  {"name": "cherry", "color": "red"}
+]
+```
+
+### Output (json-group-by color)
+
+```json
+{
+  "red": [
+    {"color": "red", "name": "apple"},
+    {"color": "red", "name": "cherry"}
+  ],
+  "yellow": [
+    {"color": "yellow", "name": "banana"}
+  ]
+}
+```
+
+## Exit Codes
+
+| Code | Meaning                    |
