+# json-flatten-keys
+
+Flatten nested JSON keys into a single level.
+
+```bash
+echo '{"a": {"b": {"c": 1}}}' | json-flatten-keys
+# Output: {"a.b.c": 1}
+```
+
+## Install
+
+```bash
+go install github.com/TataneSan/json-flatten-keys@latest
+```
+
+Or build from source:
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/json-flatten-keys.git
+cd json-flatten-keys
+go build -o json-flatten-keys .
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```
+json-flatten-keys [flags]
+```
+
+### Flags
+
+| Flag | Default | Description |
+|------|---------|-------------|
+| `-s` | `.` | Separator for flattened keys |
+| `-f` | | Input file (default: stdin) |
+| `-o` | | Output file (default: stdout) |
+| `-c` | | Compact output (no indentation) |
+| `-p` | | Prefix for all keys |
+| `-d` | `0` | Max nesting depth to flatten (0 = unlimited) |
+
+## Examples
+
+### Basic flattening
+
+```bash
+echo '{"user": {"name": {"first": "John", "last": "Doe"}}}' | json-flatten-keys
+```
+
+Output:
+```json
+{
+  "user.name.first": "John",
+  "user.name.last": "Doe"
+}
+```
+
+### Custom separator
+
+```bash
+echo '{"config": {"db": {"host": "localhost"}}}' | json-flatten-keys -s /
+```
+
+Output:
+```json
+{
+  "config/db/host": "localhost"
+}
+```
+
+### With arrays
+
+```bash
+echo '{"items": [{"id": 1}, {"id": 2}]}' | json-flatten-keys
+```
+
+Output:
+```json
+{
