+# path-exists
+
+Check if files or directories exist. Returns exit code 0 if paths exist, 1 otherwise.
+
+```bash
+path-exists /etc/passwd /tmp /nonexistent
+[EXISTS] (file) /etc/passwd
+[EXISTS] (directory) /tmp
+[NOT FOUND] /nonexistent
+```
+
+## Install
+
+```bash
+go install github.com/TataneSan/path-exists@latest
+```
+
+Or build from source:
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/path-exists.git
+cd path-exists
+go build -o path-exists .
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```
+path-exists [flags] <path> [path...]
+```
+
+### Flags
+
+| Flag | Default | Description |
+|------|---------|-------------|
+| `-f` | | Check if path is a file |
+| `-d` | | Check if path is a directory |
+| `-l` | | Check if path is a symlink |
+| `-j` | | Output as JSON |
+| `-v` | | Verbose output with details |
+| `-a` | | Exit 0 only if ALL paths exist (default: any) |
+
+## Examples
+
+### Check multiple paths
+
+```bash
+path-exists /etc/passwd /tmp /var/log
+```
+
+### Verbose output
+
+```bash
+path-exists -v /etc/passwd /tmp
+/etc/passwd: EXISTS (file, 1766 bytes, -rw-r--r--)
+/tmp: EXISTS (directory, 24576 bytes, drwxrwxrwt)
+```
+
+### JSON output
+
+```bash
+path-exists -j /etc/passwd
+```
+
+Output:
+```json
+[
+  {"path":"/etc/passwd", "exists":true, "is_file":true, "is_dir":false, "is_link":false, "size":1766, "mode":"-rw-r--r--", "error":""}
+]
+```
+
+### Use in shell scripts
+
+```bash
+if path-exists /etc/config.yml; then
+    echo "Config found"
+fi
+```
