+# json-unique
+
+Remove duplicate elements from a JSON array.
+
+## Install
+
+```bash
+go install github.com/TataneSan/json-unique@latest
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```
+json-unique [flags]
+```
+
+## Flags
+
+| Flag | Default | Description |
+|------|---------|-------------|
+| `-i` | | Input file (default: stdin) |
+| `-o` | | Output file (default: stdout) |
+| `-k` | | Deduplicate by key (for arrays of objects) |
+| `-p` | `true` | Pretty-print output |
+
+## Examples
+
+Remove duplicates from a flat array:
+```bash
+echo '[1,2,3,2,1,4]' | json-unique
+```
+
+Deduplicate objects by a key:
+```bash
+json-unique -k id -i users.json
+```
+
+Compact output (no pretty-print):
+```bash
+echo '[1,2,2,3]' | json-unique -p=false
+```
+
+From file to file:
+```bash
+json-unique -k name -i input.json -o output.json
+```
+
+## Input
+
+```json
+[
+  {"id": 1, "name": "Alice"},
+  {"id": 2, "name": "Bob"},
+  {"id": 1, "name": "Alice"},
+  {"id": 3, "name": "Charlie"}
+]
+```
+
+```bash
+$ json-unique -k id -i users.json
+```
+
+Output:
+```json
+[
+  {"id": 1, "name": "Alice"},
+  {"id": 2, "name": "Bob"},
+  {"id": 3, "name": "Charlie"}
+]
+```
+
+## License
+
+MIT
