+# csv-validate
+
+Validate CSV file structure from the command line.
+
+Checks column count consistency and empty fields.
+
+## Install
+
+```bash
+go install github.com/TataneSan/csv-validate@latest
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```
+csv-validate [flags] file.csv [file2.csv ...]
+```
+
+## Flags
+
+| Flag | Default | Description |
+|------|---------|-------------|
+| `-columns` | `0` | Expected column count (0 = auto from header) |
+| `-d` | `,` | Field delimiter |
+
+## Examples
+
+Validate a CSV file:
+```bash
+csv-validate data.csv
+```
+
+Validate multiple files:
+```bash
+csv-validate file1.csv file2.csv
+```
+
+Validate with tab delimiter:
+```bash
+csv-validate -d $'\t' data.tsv
+```
+
+Enforce column count:
+```bash
+csv-validate -columns 5 data.csv
+```
+
+## Exit codes
+
+- `0` — all files valid
+- `1` — validation errors found
+
+## License
+
+MIT
