+# ncat-lite
+
+A lightweight TCP client and server written in Go. Useful for debugging network connections, testing services, and transferring data over TCP.
+
+## Features
+
+- **Client mode**: Connect to any TCP server
+- **Server mode**: Listen for incoming connections
+- **Hex dump**: View data in hex + ASCII format
+- **Timeout support**: Configurable connection timeouts
+- **Connection limits**: Accept a fixed number of connections then exit
+- **Pipe-friendly**: Works with stdin/stdout for scripting
+
+## Install
+
+### From source
+
+```bash
+go install github.com/TataneSan/ncat-lite@latest
+```
+
+### Build locally
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/ncat-lite.git
+cd ncat-lite
+go build -o ncat-lite .
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```
+ncat-lite [options] <host> <port>    Connect to a TCP server
+ncat-lite -l [options] <port>        Listen for incoming connections
+```
+
+### Options
+
+| Flag | Description |
+|------|-------------|
+| `-l` | Listen mode (start a TCP server) |
+| `-s <addr>` | Address to bind to (default: `0.0.0.0`) |
+| `-c <count>` | Close after N connections (listen mode) |
+| `-t <seconds>` | Timeout in seconds (0 = no timeout) |
+| `-x` | Hex dump mode (show hex + ASCII) |
+| `-q` | Quiet mode (suppress status messages) |
+| `-v` | Verbose mode |
+| `-V` | Show version |
+
+## Examples
+
+### Connect to a server
+
+```bash
+# Interactive connection
+ncat-lite example.com 80
+
+# Send an HTTP request
+echo -e "GET / HTTP/1.0\r\n\r\n" | ncat-lite example.com 80
+
+# With timeout
+ncat-lite -t 5 -v example.com 443
+```
+
+### Listen for connections
+
+```bash
+# Simple listener on port 8080
+ncat-lite -l 8080
+
+# Accept only 3 connections then exit
+ncat-lite -l -c 3 8080
+
+# Bind to localhost only
+ncat-lite -l -s 127.0.0.1 9090
+```
+
+### Hex dump mode
