+# csv-cut
+
+Extract specific columns from CSV files. A fast Go CLI tool for selecting and outputting columns by index.
+
+## Features
+
+- Extract single or multiple columns by 1-indexed position
+- Custom input/output delimiters (comma, semicolon, tab, pipe, etc.)
+- Header handling (skip or auto-print)
+- Whitespace stripping
+- Reads from file or stdin (pipe-friendly)
+
+## Install
+
+```bash
+go install github.com/TataneSan/csv-cut@latest
+```
+
+Or build locally:
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/csv-cut.git
+cd csv-cut
+go build -o csv-cut .
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```
+csv-cut -c <columns> [options] [file]
+```
+
+### Options
+
+| Flag | Description |
+|------|-------------|
+| `-c <cols>` | Columns to extract (1-indexed, comma-separated) |
+| `-f <char>` | Input delimiter (default: `,`) |
+| `-d <char>` | Output delimiter (default: same as input) |
+| `-H` | Skip header row |
+| `-h` | Print a header row with column names |
+| `-s` | Strip whitespace from fields |
+| `-V` | Show version |
+
+## Examples
+
+```bash
+# Extract columns 1 and 3
+csv-cut -c 1,3 data.csv
+
+# Extract column 2 from semicolon-separated file
+csv-cut -c 2 -f ';' data.csv
+
+# Extract columns, skip header, output as TSV
+csv-cut -c 1,2,4 -H -d $'\t' data.csv
+
+# Pipe from stdin
+cat data.csv | csv-cut -c 5
+
+# Extract and strip whitespace
+csv-cut -c 1,3 -s data.csv
+```
+
+## License
+
+MIT
