+# file-touch
+
+Create or update file timestamps in batch. Supports glob patterns, reference files, and multiple time formats.
+
+## Features
+
+- Set specific timestamps on files
+- Copy timestamps from a reference file
+- Create files if they don't exist (`-f`)
+- Glob pattern expansion
+- Change access time (`-a`) or modify time (`-m`) independently
+
+## Install
+
+```bash
+go install github.com/TataneSan/file-touch@latest
+```
+
+Or build locally:
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/file-touch.git
+cd file-touch
+go build -o file-touch .
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```bash
+# Touch files with current time
+file-touch file1.txt file2.txt
+
+# Set specific time
+file-touch -t "2024-01-15 14:30:00" *.log
+
+# Copy timestamps from reference file
+file-touch -r reference.txt target1.txt target2.txt
+
+# Create files if missing
+file-touch -f -t "2024-06-01" new-file.txt
+
+# Change only access time
+file-touch -a -t "2024-03-15 10:00" file.txt
+
+# Change only modify time
+file-touch -m -t "2024-03-15 10:00" file.txt
+
+# Glob patterns
+file-touch -t "2024-01-01" /var/log/app-*.log
+```
+
+## License
+
+MIT
