+# file-rename-batch
+
+Batch rename files with regex patterns, case conversion, and string replacement.
+
+## Features
+
+- **Regex find & replace** — rename files using regex patterns with capture groups
+- **Case conversion** — upper, lower, title, camelCase, snake_case, kebab-case
+- **Dry run** — preview changes before applying (`--dry-run`)
+- **Recursive** — process subdirectories (`--recursive`)
+- **Extension filter** — only rename files with a specific extension (`--ext .txt`)
+- **Reverse order** — process files in reverse alphabetical order
+
+## Install
+
+```bash
+go install github.com/TataneSan/file-rename-batch@latest
+```
+
+Or build from source:
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/file-rename-batch.git
+cd file-rename-batch
+go build -o file-rename-batch .
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```
+file-rename-batch [FLAGS] [TARGETS...]
+```
+
+### Flags
+
+| Flag | Alias | Description |
+|------|-------|-------------|
+| `--find PATTERN` | `-f` | Regex pattern to match in filenames |
+| `--replace STRING` | `-r` | Replacement string (use `$1`, `$2` for groups) |
+| `--case MODE` | `-c` | Case conversion: `upper`, `lower`, `title`, `camel`, `snake`, `kebab` |
+| `--dry-run` | `-n` | Preview changes without renaming |
+| `--recursive` | `-R` | Process subdirectories recursively |
+| `--ext EXT` | `-e` | Only process files with this extension |
+| `--reverse` | | Process files in reverse order |
+
+## Examples
+
+### Replace text in filenames
+
+```bash
+# Replace "report" with "summary" in all files
+file-rename-batch -f "report" -r "summary"
+
+# Replace dates: 2024-01-15 -> 20240115
+file-rename-batch -f "([0-9]{4})-([0-9]{2})-([0-9]{2})" -r "$1$2$3"
+```
+
+### Case conversion
+
+```bash
+# Convert all files to uppercase
+file-rename-batch -c upper
+
+# Convert to snake_case
+file-rename-batch -c snake
+
+# Convert to camelCase
+file-rename-batch -c camel
+
+# Convert to kebab-case
+file-rename-batch -c kebab
+```
+
+### Combine regex + case
+
+```bash
+# Remove "draft-" prefix and convert to lowercase
+file-rename-batch -f "^draft-" -r "" -c lower
