+# json-to-xml
+
+Convert JSON data to well-formed XML from the command line.
+
+## Install
+
+```bash
+go install github.com/TataneSan/json-to-xml@latest
+```
+
+Or build from source:
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/json-to-xml.git
+cd json-to-xml
+go build -o json-to-xml .
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```
+json-to-xml [flags] [file]
+cat data.json | json-to-xml
+```
+
+## Flags
+
+| Flag | Description | Default |
+|------|-------------|---------|
+| `--root NAME` | Root element name | `root` |
+| `--array-element NAME` | Name for array items | `item` |
+| `--pretty` | Pretty-print XML output | compact |
+| `-v, --version` | Show version | — |
+| `-h, --help` | Show help | — |
+
+## Examples
+
+### Basic conversion
+
+```bash
+echo '{"name":"Alice","age":30}' | json-to-xml
+# <root><age>30</age><name>Alice</name></root>
+```
+
+### Custom root element
+
+```bash
+echo '{"name":"Alice","age":30}' | json-to-xml --root person
+# <person><age>30</age><name>Alice</name></person>
+```
+
+### Pretty-print with nested objects and arrays
+
+```bash
+echo '{"name":"Alice","skills":["Go","Rust"],"address":{"city":"Paris"}}' | json-to-xml --pretty --root user
+```
+
+```xml
+<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
+<user>
+  <address>
+    <city>Paris</city>
+  </address>
+  <name>Alice</name>
+  <skills>
+    <item>Go</item>
+    <item>Rust</item>
+  </skills>
+</user>
+```
+
+### Custom array element name
+
+```bash
+echo '{"users":[{"name":"Alice"},{"name":"Bob"}]}' | json-to-xml --root data --array-element user
+# <data><users><user><name>Alice</name></user><user><name>Bob</name></user></users></data>
+```
+
