+# toml-to-ini
+
+Convert TOML files to INI format from the command line.
+
+## Install
+
+```bash
+go install github.com/TataneSan/toml-to-ini@latest
+```
+
+Or build from source:
+
+```bash
+git clone https://github.com/TataneSan/toml-to-ini.git
+cd toml-to-ini
+go build -o toml-to-ini .
+```
+
+## Usage
+
+```
+toml-to-ini [flags] [file]
+cat config.toml | toml-to-ini
+```
+
+## Flags
+
+| Flag | Description | Default |
+|------|-------------|---------|
+| `--pretty` | Add extra spacing between sections | compact |
+| `-v, --version` | Show version | — |
+| `-h, --help` | Show help | — |
+
+## Examples
+
+### Basic conversion
+
+```bash
+toml-to-ini config.toml
+```
+
+```ini
+[database]
+host = localhost
+port = 5432
+enabled = true
+
+[server]
+name = myapp
+debug = false
+```
+
+### Pretty output
+
+```bash
+toml-to-ini --pretty config.toml
+```
+
+### Pipe from stdin
+
+```bash
+cat config.toml | toml-to-ini
+```
+
+### Pipe from HTTP
+
+```bash
+curl -s https://example.com/config.toml | toml-to-ini
+```
+
+## Features
+
+- Reads TOML from file or stdin
+- Supports sections, key-value pairs, booleans, integers, floats, strings
+- Handles arrays and inline tables
+- Sorted keys for deterministic output
+- Proper INI quoting for strings with special characters
+- Pretty-print mode with extra spacing
